  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Structuring the Codebase**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a modular application architecture. I\'ve begun organizing the codebase, and have defined key types in `/src/types.ts`, which includes household profiles, member details, and dietary preferences. I\'m moving toward defining nutrient targets, like protein and vitamins, as well as meal planning components.\n\n\n**Defining Data Requirements**\n\nI\'m now identifying the crucial datasets. I\'ve begun detailing nutrient compositions and farm profiles. Crop yield model inputs and market price forecasts are also priorities. I\'m considering user profiles and data sources, which will be essential for provenance and system transparency.\n\n\n**Gathering Data Assets**\n\nI\'ve just added several data assets. I\'m importing `ifct2017_nutrition.ts`, with detailed nutrient breakdowns for Indian crops, as well as `agmarknet_mandi_prices.ts` containing market records. Lastly, `crop_yield_dataset.ts` will provide historical crop yield data. I\'m focusing on parsing and integrating these datasets now.\n\n\n**Designing the Agent Framework**\n\nI\'m structuring the backend agents now. I\'m building `nutrition_agent.ts` for nutrient target calculation and gap analysis. Also, I\'m integrating the `crop_planning_agent.ts` with XGBoost. I\'ve designed the `climate_agent.ts` for weather alerts and ET0 calculation and will finish market data integration for `market_agent.ts`. I am considering data provenance with `data_sources.ts`.\n\n\n**Implementing Optimization Strategies**\n\nI\'m now integrating the trend and seasonal decomposition for commodity market prices to improve the finance optimization. The new `finance_optimization_agent.ts` is a closed-loop OR-Tools LP / Simplex Harvest Allocation solver that will optimize farmer net income by satisfying family nutrition, storage capacity, and farm resource constraints. I\'m also adding `gemini_explainer.ts`, implementing a Gemini integration for natural language explanations, regional language translations, and audio readouts. Lastly, `supabase_client.ts` is in place for database persistence.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Application**\n\nI\'m now creating the application\'s user interface. I\'ve developed several key React components, including `NutritionDashboard.tsx` to visualize nutrient coverage and recommend crops, and `CropPlanCard.tsx` for crop recommendations and yield predictions. I\'ve also incorporated `ClimateWidget.tsx` for weather data and risk scores, and `MarketTrendsCard.tsx` to display market forecasts. Lastly, I\'m integrating `HarvestAllocationOptimizer.tsx` for optimization and plan summaries, as well as `GeminiAssistant.tsx`, for natural language explanation of farm plans.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 12
      nanos: 603894695
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
