  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the UI**\n\nI\'m currently focused on constructing the frontend UI components within the `/src/components/` directory and handling state management in `/src/App.tsx`. The design\'s visual identity leans towards a sophisticated neutral color scheme with high contrast. I\'m incorporating emerald green accents, specifically using `emerald-700` and `emerald-600`, to highlight the themes of agriculture and nutrition resilience.\n\n\n**Defining Component Architecture**\n\nI\'m now deep in defining the required UI components, breaking them down by functionality. The `Navbar` is taking shape with all the necessary elements: logo, tagline, status badge, scenario switcher, navigation tabs, and auth button. We also have a `DemoBanner` component which will highlight anti-hallucination rules compliance. I\'m focusing on interactive cards to demo the flow.\n\n\n**Integrating Data Sources**\n\nI\'ve been integrating external data sources, specifically the MR-NIN IFCT 2017 Nutrition Database, Open-Meteo for weather, AGMARKNET for market prices. I\'m also incorporating the XGBoost crop yield model and Prophet for price forecasting, along with OR-Tools for harvest allocation.\n\nI am developing the UI components to align with these data sources and models.\nI am implementing the FarmerProfileWizard.tsx component with form inputs for relevant farmer and land information, incorporating a \"Populate Demo Scenario\" option.\nFurthermore, I\'m working on the NutritionDashboard.tsx, which will feature interactive nutrition progress visuals, and the CropPlanCard.tsx with XGBoost recommendations and planting calendar interactivity.\n\n\n**Developing Key Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on several critical components. I\'ve got the `ClimateWidget.tsx` using live Open-Meteo data, complete with actionable alerts. The `MarketTrendsCard.tsx` is showcasing price trends against the Prophet forecast, including recommendations. I\'m also implementing the `HarvestAllocationOptimizer.tsx` using OR-Tools, and it\'s producing closed-loop results for different allocation scenarios. Finally, I\'m integrating the `GeminiAssistant.tsx` with regional language support.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 14122004
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
