    response: "I have completed the requested backend integrations and user experience enhancements for NutriHarvest AI:\n\n### Key Work Accomplished:\n- **Supabase Authentication & Persistent Sessions**:\n  - **Full Auth Flow**: Integrated sign-up, sign-in, and sign-out logic in `SupabaseService` and `AuthModal`.\n  - **Session Restoration**: Configured `SupabaseService.onAuthStateChange` and `getSession()` listeners in `App.tsx` so user sessions persist seamlessly across browser tab reloads and app restarts.\n  - **Environment Key Safety**: Secured Supabase credentials using environment variables (`VITE_SUPABASE_URL`, `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`) with graceful fallback handling for local offline sessions.\n\n- **4-Step Guided Onboarding Flow (`FarmerProfileWizard`)**:\n  - **Step 1 (Demographics)**: Collects farmer name, dietary choices (Vegetarian, Eggetarian, Non-Veg, Vegan), and auto-calculated household member age breakdowns (0\342\200\2235 yrs, 6\342\200\22312 yrs, 13\342\200\22318 yrs, 19\342\200\22359 yrs, 60+ yrs).\n  - **Step 2 (Geography & Inputs)**: Captures state, district, farm acreage, water source (borewell, canal, rainfed, micro-drip), and seasonal input budget in \342\202\271.\n  - **Step 3 (Soil & Crop History)**: Records soil type, pH level, N-P-K nutrient values, organic carbon, and a multi-select crop history grid.\n  - **Step 4 (Personalization Review & DB Persistence)**: Summarizes all inputs and saves the profile directly to the Supabase database (`farmer_onboarding` and `profiles` tables). Includes step-by-step validation and inline error alerts.\n\n- **Real-Time Open-Meteo Weather Integration**:\n  - **`WeatherProvider` Interface**: Built `OpenMeteoWeatherProvider` implementing real-time REST API calls to Open-Meteo for temperature, precipitation, humidity, wind speed, and FAO ET0 evapotranspiration.\n  - **15-Min TTL Caching**: Added multi-tier caching (in-memory & `localStorage`) to optimize API rate limits and ensure continuous availability offline.\n  - **Rule-Based Climate Engine**: Automated actionable irrigation schedules (e.g., pausing canal pumps during 60%+ rain forecasts) and heat alerts, wired directly into `ClimateAgent` and the `ExecutiveDashboard`."
