  planner_response {
    response: "All requested features have been fully implemented, integrated, and verified:\n\n### Summary of Implementation\n\n#### 1. User Authentication & Profile Persistence (Supabase Auth)\n- **Authentication Flows**: Built full sign-up, sign-in, and sign-out capabilities in `SupabaseService` (`src/backend/supabase_service.ts`) and `AuthModal` (`src/components/AuthModal.tsx`).\n- **Session Restoration**: Added `onAuthStateChange` listeners and `getSession()` initialization in `App.tsx` so user sessions persist across page refreshes and browser restarts.\n- **Protected User Profiles**: Automatically syncs user credentials and onboarding profiles with Supabase database tables (`profiles` and `farmer_onboarding`) with fallback to local storage for offline operation.\n- **Secure Credentials**: Credentials managed via environment variables (`VITE_SUPABASE_URL`, `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`).\n\n#### 2. Guided Onboarding Flow (`FarmerProfileWizard`)\n- **4-Step Interactive Configurator**:\n  1. **Demographics**: Farmer name, dietary choices (Vegetarian, Eggetarian, Non-Veg, Vegan), and household member breakdown across 5 age groups (0\342\200\2235, 6\342\200\22312, 13\342\200\22318, 19\342\200\22359, 60+ yrs).\n  2. **Geography & Budget**: State, district, land acreage, seasonal input budget (\342\202\271), and water availability (borewell, canal, rainfed, drip).\n  3. **Soil & History**: Soil type, pH, N-P-K nutrient parameters, organic carbon, and interactive multi-select crop history.\n  4. **Review & Data Sync**: Summary card with inline validation error handling and direct persistence into Supabase database.\n- Integrated seamlessly into the top bar navigation with progress indicators.\n\n#### 3. Real-Time Open-Meteo Weather Integration (`WeatherProvider`)\n- **Connector**: Built `OpenMeteoWeatherProvider` (`src/backend/weather_provider.ts`) implementing the `WeatherProvider` interface.\n- **Live Data**: Fetches real-time temperature, precipitation sum & probability, humidity, wind speed, and FAO ET0 evapotranspiration from the Open-Meteo REST API.\n- **15-Minute Caching**: Features in-memory and `localStorage` caching with a 15-minute TTL to optimize API rate limits and enable offline fallback.\n- **Climate & Irrigation Engine**: Evaluates transparent rules for irrigation pausing (during >60% rain forecast), drip volume recommendations, and field heat stress alerts.\n\n#### 4. `DATA_GOV_API_KEY` Removal & Verification\n- **Codebase Audit**: Inspected the repository and confirmed no runtime code depends on `DATA_GOV_API_KEY`.\n- **Local Dataset**: Updated `.env.example` to mark `DATA_GOV_API_KEY` as completely optional and verified that the `MarketAgent` runs reliably using the local AGMARKNET dataset in `src/data/agmarknet_mandi_prices.ts`."
    modified_response: "All requested features have been fully implemented, integrated, and verified:\n\n### Summary of Implementation\n\n#### 1. User Authentication & Profile Persistence (Supabase Auth)\n- **Authentication Flows**: Built full sign-up, sign-in, and sign-out capabilities in `SupabaseService` (`src/backend/supabase_service.ts`) and `AuthModal` (`src/components/AuthModal.tsx`).\n- **Session Restoration**: Added `onAuthStateChange` listeners and `getSession()` initialization in `App.tsx` so user sessions persist across page refreshes and browser restarts.\n- **Protected User Profiles**: Automatically syncs user credentials and onboarding profiles with Supabase database tables (`profiles` and `farmer_onboarding`) with fallback to local storage for offline operation.\n- **Secure Credentials**: Credentials managed via environment variables (`VITE_SUPABASE_URL`, `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`).\n\n#### 2. Guided Onboarding Flow (`FarmerProfileWizard`)\n- **4-Step Interactive Configurator**:\n  1. **Demographics**: Farmer name, dietary choices (Vegetarian, Eggetarian, Non-Veg, Vegan), and household member breakdown across 5 age groups (0\342\200\2235, 6\342\200\22312, 13\342\200\22318, 19\342\200\22359, 60+ yrs).\n  2. **Geography & Budget**: State, district, land acreage, seasonal input budget (\342\202\271), and water availability (borewell, canal, rainfed, drip).\n  3. **Soil & History**: Soil type, pH, N-P-K nutrient parameters, organic carbon, and interactive multi-select crop history.\n  4. **Review & Data Sync**: Summary card with inline validation error handling and direct persistence into Supabase database.\n- Integrated seamlessly into the top bar navigation with progress indicators.\n\n#### 3. Real-Time Open-Meteo Weather Integration (`WeatherProvider`)\n- **Connector**: Built `OpenMeteoWeatherProvider` (`src/backend/weather_provider.ts`) implementing the `WeatherProvider` interface.\n- **Live Data**: Fetches real-time temperature, precipitation sum & probability, humidity, wind speed, and FAO ET0 evapotranspiration from the Open-Meteo REST API.\n- **15-Minute Caching**: Features in-memory and `localStorage` caching with a 15-minute TTL to optimize API rate limits and enable offline fallback.\n- **Climate & Irrigation Engine**: Evaluates transparent rules for irrigation pausing (during >60% rain forecast), drip volume recommendations, and field heat stress alerts.\n\n#### 4. `DATA_GOV_API_KEY` Removal & Verification\n- **Codebase Audit**: Inspected the repository and confirmed no runtime code depends on `DATA_GOV_API_KEY`.\n- **Local Dataset**: Updated `.env.example` to mark `DATA_GOV_API_KEY` as completely optional and verified that the `MarketAgent` runs reliably using the local AGMARKNET dataset in `src/data/agmarknet_mandi_prices.ts`."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
