  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Update the app flow so it follows a **standard modern app onboarding and authentication experience**.\n\n### 1. Intro / Landing Page\n\nWhen a user opens the app for the first time, show a clean and professional **intro/landing page** before showing any app features.\n\nThe intro page should:\n\n* Display the app logo/name prominently.\n* Briefly explain what the app does and its main benefits.\n* Have a clear **Get Started** button.\n* Have a professional, modern UI consistent with the rest of the application.\n* Do **not** show the main app dashboard or protected features before authentication.\n\n### 2. Authentication Required\n\nWhen the user clicks **Get Started**, take them to the authentication screen.\n\nThe user must be able to:\n\n* **Sign Up**\n* **Log In**\n* **Log Out**\n\nUse the existing Supabase Auth implementation.\n\nAuthentication must persist across app restarts/refreshes, and the app should correctly detect whether a user is already authenticated.\n\n### 3. Mandatory Profile / Onboarding\n\nAfter a user successfully signs up or logs in for the first time, they must complete the **onboarding/profile form** before accessing the main application.\n\nCollect all required information, such as:\n\n* Household size\n* Age groups\n* Dietary preferences\n* Farm size\n* Location\n* Water availability\n* Soil information\n* Crop/farming details\n* Any other information already defined in the application\'s onboarding requirements\n\nStore this information securely in the Supabase database and associate it with the authenticated user\'s ID.\n\n### 4. Enforce the Correct Flow\n\nThe application must enforce this sequence:\n\n**First-time user:**\n`Intro Page \342\206\222 Sign Up \342\206\222 Complete Onboarding/Profile \342\206\222 Main Dashboard \342\206\222 App Features`\n\n**Existing user with completed profile:**\n`Intro Page \342\206\222 Login \342\206\222 Main Dashboard \342\206\222 App Features`\n\n**Existing user who has not completed onboarding:**\n`Intro Page \342\206\222 Login \342\206\222 Complete Onboarding/Profile \342\206\222 Main Dashboard \342\206\222 App Features`\n\n### 5. Protected Routes\n\nAll actual application features must be protected.\n\nA user must **NOT** be able to access:\n\n* Dashboard\n* Farming recommendations\n* AI features\n* Simulations\n* Profile-dependent features\n* Any other authenticated functionality\n\nuntil they are both:\n\n1. Authenticated, and\n2. Have completed the required onboarding/profile information.\n\nIf an unauthenticated user tries to access a protected route, redirect them to the Login page.\n\nIf an authenticated user has incomplete onboarding, redirect them to the Onboarding page.\n\n### 6. Returning Users\n\nDo not force returning users to fill out the onboarding form again if their profile is already complete.\n\nAfter authentication, check the user\'s profile/onboarding completion status and automatically route them to the correct screen.\n\n### 7. UX Requirements\n\nMake the entire flow feel like a real production application:\n\n* Smooth page transitions.\n* Loading states while checking authentication.\n* Proper error handling.\n* Clear validation messages.\n* Responsive design for desktop and mobile.\n* No flash of the protected dashboard while authentication is being checked.\n* Preserve the existing design system, colors, typography, and components.\n* Do not remove or break any existing features.\n\n### Important\n\nDo not simply hide the features from the UI. **Actually enforce authentication and onboarding at the routing/application level**, so users cannot bypass the flow by manually entering a protected URL.\n\nImplement this complete flow using the existing Supabase Auth and database setup, while keeping all existing functionality intact."
    items {
      text: "Update the app flow so it follows a **standard modern app onboarding and authentication experience**.\n\n### 1. Intro / Landing Page\n\nWhen a user opens the app for the first time, show a clean and professional **intro/landing page** before showing any app features.\n\nThe intro page should:\n\n* Display the app logo/name prominently.\n* Briefly explain what the app does and its main benefits.\n* Have a clear **Get Started** button.\n* Have a professional, modern UI consistent with the rest of the application.\n* Do **not** show the main app dashboard or protected features before authentication.\n\n### 2. Authentication Required\n\nWhen the user clicks **Get Started**, take them to the authentication screen.\n\nThe user must be able to:\n\n* **Sign Up**\n* **Log In**\n* **Log Out**\n\nUse the existing Supabase Auth implementation.\n\nAuthentication must persist across app restarts/refreshes, and the app should correctly detect whether a user is already authenticated.\n\n### 3. Mandatory Profile / Onboarding\n\nAfter a user successfully signs up or logs in for the first time, they must complete the **onboarding/profile form** before accessing the main application.\n\nCollect all required information, such as:\n\n* Household size\n* Age groups\n* Dietary preferences\n* Farm size\n* Location\n* Water availability\n* Soil information\n* Crop/farming details\n* Any other information already defined in the application\'s onboarding requirements\n\nStore this information securely in the Supabase database and associate it with the authenticated user\'s ID.\n\n### 4. Enforce the Correct Flow\n\nThe application must enforce this sequence:\n\n**First-time user:**\n`Intro Page \342\206\222 Sign Up \342\206\222 Complete Onboarding/Profile \342\206\222 Main Dashboard \342\206\222 App Features`\n\n**Existing user with completed profile:**\n`Intro Page \342\206\222 Login \342\206\222 Main Dashboard \342\206\222 App Features`\n\n**Existing user who has not completed onboarding:**\n`Intro Page \342\206\222 Login \342\206\222 Complete Onboarding/Profile \342\206\222 Main Dashboard \342\206\222 App Features`\n\n### 5. Protected Routes\n\nAll actual application features must be protected.\n\nA user must **NOT** be able to access:\n\n* Dashboard\n* Farming recommendations\n* AI features\n* Simulations\n* Profile-dependent features\n* Any other authenticated functionality\n\nuntil they are both:\n\n1. Authenticated, and\n2. Have completed the required onboarding/profile information.\n\nIf an unauthenticated user tries to access a protected route, redirect them to the Login page.\n\nIf an authenticated user has incomplete onboarding, redirect them to the Onboarding page.\n\n### 6. Returning Users\n\nDo not force returning users to fill out the onboarding form again if their profile is already complete.\n\nAfter authentication, check the user\'s profile/onboarding completion status and automatically route them to the correct screen.\n\n### 7. UX Requirements\n\nMake the entire flow feel like a real production application:\n\n* Smooth page transitions.\n* Loading states while checking authentication.\n* Proper error handling.\n* Clear validation messages.\n* Responsive design for desktop and mobile.\n* No flash of the protected dashboard while authentication is being checked.\n* Preserve the existing design system, colors, typography, and components.\n* Do not remove or break any existing features.\n\n### Important\n\nDo not simply hide the features from the UI. **Actually enforce authentication and onboarding at the routing/application level**, so users cannot bypass the flow by manually entering a protected URL.\n\nImplement this complete flow using the existing Supabase Auth and database setup, while keeping all existing functionality intact."
    }
