    thinking: "**Analyzing Flow Components**\n\nI\'m currently breaking down the required flow components, focusing on constructing them robustly. I\'m starting with the landing page (`LandingPage.tsx`) as a dedicated component, ensuring a clean and organized structure. I\'m aiming for modularity in this initial stage, so I can ensure proper component implementation.\n\n\n**Defining Landing Page Elements**\n\nI\'ve specified the components of the landing page: Hero section with branding, tagline, and headline; primary CTAs (\"Get Started\", \"Log In\"); and a feature highlights grid. The grid will feature key benefits like ICMR nutrition alignment and hyperlocal weather data using Open-Meteo. I am also planning on including AGMARKNET price forecasting and OR-Tools harvest allocation.\n\n\n**Defining Security & UI**\n\nI\'m now integrating security with Supabase Auth and RLS, incorporating verified government data. I am also working on modernizing the UI with natural tones and specific font selections. I want a polished and approachable look.\n**Creating Auth Flow**\n\nI\'ve sketched out the authentication flow: A dedicated view/modal for login and signup. After successful authentication, it updates the session and checks profile completion. If the profile is completed it will route to the dashboard and if not, it will route to onboarding.\n\n\n**Implementing Onboarding Profile**\n\nI\'m now detailing the user onboarding profile information: household size, dietary preferences, farm details, and budget. This will save to the Supabase database. The onboarding flow will then set a completed status, and direct the user to the dashboard.\n\n**Defining App State**\n\nI\'m working on defining the app states within `App.tsx`. I am defining states for authentication status (checking auth, session data), and a flag to manage the onboarding completion status. The system will check the session at boot and proceed accordingly.\n\n\n**Enforcing Authentication & Onboarding**\n\nI\'m implementing route protection in `App.tsx` based on login and onboarding completion. If the user isn\'t logged in, only the landing page or auth components render, with any protected feature redirects going to login. If logged in but onboarding isn\'t done, the `FarmerProfileWizard` appears with a prominent banner to guide the process. This ensures a consistent and controlled user experience.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 410565100
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
