  planner_response {
    response: "I have resolved the `Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading \'includes\')` error.\n\n### Root Cause\nThe `farm.cropHistory` array property was being accessed directly via `.includes(cropName)` in step 3 of the `FarmerProfileWizard` component without checking if `cropHistory` was defined. If a user profile loaded with `cropHistory` unset or `undefined` (such as when parsing legacy cached state or partial profile data), calling `.includes` threw a runtime `TypeError`.\n\n### Fixes Applied\n1. **Safe Array Access in `FarmerProfileWizard.tsx`**:\n   - Replaced direct `farm.cropHistory.includes(cropName)` calls with safe fallback array chaining: `(farm.cropHistory || []).includes(cropName)`.\n   - Updated `toggleCropHistory` to spread safely: `[...(farm.cropHistory || [])]`.\n   - Protected `.length` validation and `.join()` text output against `undefined`.\n   - Added safe navigation operators for `farm.soil` and `farmer.ageGroups`.\n\n2. **Market Agent Safeguard (`market_agent.ts`)**:\n   - Added null-checks on `r.commodity` and `r.state` before running `.toLowerCase().includes()`.\n\n3. **Data Sanitization (`supabase_service.ts`)**:\n   - Added automatic array initialization for `localData.farm.cropHistory` upon loading profile data from storage."
    thinking: "**Reviewing Code Changes**\n\nI\'ve just finished reviewing the code changes, and it looks like both `lint_applet` and `compile_applet` passed without any issues. Specifically, I added optional chaining and safe array handling in `FarmerProfileWizard.tsx` for `cropHistory`, and tested the fixes.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have resolved the `Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading \'includes\')` error.\n\n### Root Cause\nThe `farm.cropHistory` array property was being accessed directly via `.includes(cropName)` in step 3 of the `FarmerProfileWizard` component without checking if `cropHistory` was defined. If a user profile loaded with `cropHistory` unset or `undefined` (such as when parsing legacy cached state or partial profile data), calling `.includes` threw a runtime `TypeError`.\n\n### Fixes Applied\n1. **Safe Array Access in `FarmerProfileWizard.tsx`**:\n   - Replaced direct `farm.cropHistory.includes(cropName)` calls with safe fallback array chaining: `(farm.cropHistory || []).includes(cropName)`.\n   - Updated `toggleCropHistory` to spread safely: `[...(farm.cropHistory || [])]`.\n   - Protected `.length` validation and `.join()` text output against `undefined`.\n   - Added safe navigation operators for `farm.soil` and `farmer.ageGroups`.\n\n2. **Market Agent Safeguard (`market_agent.ts`)**:\n   - Added null-checks on `r.commodity` and `r.state` before running `.toLowerCase().includes()`.\n\n3. **Data Sanitization (`supabase_service.ts`)**:\n   - Added automatic array initialization for `localData.farm.cropHistory` upon loading profile data from storage."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 134069756
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
