steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1786463780
      nanos: 736877683
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Fix a critical authentication/security issue in the app.\n\n### Current problems\n\nThere are two problems:\n\n1. When an existing user logs in again, their previously saved profile/onboarding information is not restored and they are asked to enter everything again.\n2. More importantly, when I enter an email/account that has **never signed up**, the app still allows me to enter the application and access features.\n\nThe second issue must be fixed immediately.\n\n### Required authentication behavior\n\nThe app must strictly enforce this flow:\n\n**New user:**\n`Intro \342\206\222 Sign Up \342\206\222 Account Created \342\206\222 Onboarding \342\206\222 Dashboard`\n\n**Existing user:**\n`Intro \342\206\222 Login \342\206\222 Authenticate \342\206\222 Fetch Profile \342\206\222 Dashboard`\n\n**Invalid/non-existing user:**\n`Intro \342\206\222 Login \342\206\222 Authentication Fails \342\206\222 Stay on Login \342\206\222 Show Error`\n\nAn account that does not exist must **NEVER** be allowed to access the dashboard or any protected feature.\n\n### Supabase Auth\n\nUse the existing **Supabase Auth** implementation as the single source of truth for authentication.\n\nFor login:\n\n1. Call Supabase\'s login/sign-in method.\n2. Wait for the authentication response.\n3. Verify that authentication was actually successful.\n4. Verify that a valid authenticated session exists.\n5. Only then allow navigation to protected application routes.\n\nIf authentication fails, **do not navigate to the dashboard**.\n\nDisplay a clear message such as:\n\n> \"No account found or incorrect email/password. Please sign up or check your credentials.\"\n\nDo not create an account automatically during login.\n\n### Existing user profile restoration\n\nAfter successful authentication:\n\n1. Get the authenticated Supabase `user.id`.\n2. Fetch the user\'s profile from the database using `user.id`.\n3. If the profile exists and onboarding is complete:\n\n   * Restore all saved information.\n   * Skip onboarding.\n   * Navigate directly to the dashboard.\n4. If the profile is missing/incomplete:\n\n   * Navigate to onboarding.\n   * Pre-fill any existing information.\n   * Save the completed profile using the same `user.id`.\n\nThe same user must always retrieve the same profile.\n\n### Protected routes\n\nMake sure the dashboard and ALL application features are protected at the routing level.\n\nFor every protected page/component:\n\n```text\nNo authenticated session\n        \342\206\223\nRedirect to Login\n```\n\n```text\nAuthenticated session\n        \342\206\223\nCheck profile\n        \342\206\223\nProfile incomplete \342\206\222 Onboarding\nProfile complete \342\206\222 Dashboard\n```\n\nUsers must not be able to bypass authentication by:\n\n* Typing a dashboard URL directly\n* Refreshing the page\n* Opening a protected route in a new tab\n* Manipulating frontend state\n* Returning to the app after logout\n\n### Logout\n\nWhen the user logs out:\n\n* Call Supabase sign-out.\n* Clear local authentication/profile state.\n* Invalidate the current session.\n* Redirect to the Intro/Login page.\n* Make sure protected pages cannot still be accessed using stale frontend state.\n\n### Session persistence\n\nFor users who have already logged in successfully:\n\n* Persist their Supabase session across page refreshes and browser/app restarts.\n* On application startup, check the current Supabase session.\n* Show a loading screen while checking the session.\n* Do NOT temporarily show the dashboard before authentication is verified.\n\n### Important security requirement\n\nDo NOT use a frontend variable such as:\n\n```js\nisLoggedIn = true\n```\n\nas the actual authentication mechanism.\n\nThe application must rely on the **real Supabase Auth session**.\n\nDo NOT treat:\n\n* Email entered in a form\n* User ID stored in localStorage\n* A manually created profile\n* Frontend state\n* Cached onboarding data\n\nas proof that the user is authenticated.\n\nOnly a valid Supabase Auth session should grant access to protected features.\n\n### Database security\n\nAlso inspect the Supabase database policies/RLS.\n\nUsers should only be able to read and modify their own profile data.\n\nThe relationship should be:\n\n`auth.users.id \342\206\222 profiles.user_id`\n\nand the database policies should enforce that users can only access their own records.\n\n### Test these cases\n\nAfter implementing the fix, test all of these scenarios:\n\n**Test 1 \342\200\224 New account**\n`Unknown email \342\206\222 Sign Up \342\206\222 Onboarding \342\206\222 Dashboard`\n\n**Test 2 \342\200\224 Existing account**\n`Existing email/password \342\206\222 Login \342\206\222 Existing profile restored \342\206\222 Dashboard`\n\n**Test 3 \342\200\224 Wrong password**\n`Existing email + wrong password \342\206\222 Login fails \342\206\222 Stay on Login`\n\n**Test 4 \342\200\224 Non-existing account**\n`Email that has never signed up \342\206\222 Login fails \342\206\222 Stay on Login`\n\n**Test 5 \342\200\224 Logout**\n`Dashboard \342\206\222 Logout \342\206\222 Login/Intro \342\206\222 Dashboard cannot be accessed`\n\n**Test 6 \342\200\224 Refresh**\n`Logged-in user \342\206\222 Refresh \342\206\222 Session restored \342\206\222 Dashboard`\n\n**Test 7 \342\200\224 Existing user with incomplete profile**\n`Login \342\206\222 Existing partial profile \342\206\222 Onboarding \342\206\222 Complete \342\206\222 Dashboard`\n\nPlease inspect the entire existing authentication, routing, Supabase configuration, profile database logic, RLS policies, and onboarding flow. Fix the underlying issue instead of adding a UI-only workaround.\n\nDo not remove or break any existing application features."
    items {
      text: "Fix a critical authentication/security issue in the app.\n\n### Current problems\n\nThere are two problems:\n\n1. When an existing user logs in again, their previously saved profile/onboarding information is not restored and they are asked to enter everything again.\n2. More importantly, when I enter an email/account that has **never signed up**, the app still allows me to enter the application and access features.\n\nThe second issue must be fixed immediately.\n\n### Required authentication behavior\n\nThe app must strictly enforce this flow:\n\n**New user:**\n`Intro \342\206\222 Sign Up \342\206\222 Account Created \342\206\222 Onboarding \342\206\222 Dashboard`\n\n**Existing user:**\n`Intro \342\206\222 Login \342\206\222 Authenticate \342\206\222 Fetch Profile \342\206\222 Dashboard`\n\n**Invalid/non-existing user:**\n`Intro \342\206\222 Login \342\206\222 Authentication Fails \342\206\222 Stay on Login \342\206\222 Show Error`\n\nAn account that does not exist must **NEVER** be allowed to access the dashboard or any protected feature.\n\n### Supabase Auth\n\nUse the existing **Supabase Auth** implementation as the single source of truth for authentication.\n\nFor login:\n\n1. Call Supabase\'s login/sign-in method.\n2. Wait for the authentication response.\n3. Verify that authentication was actually successful.\n4. Verify that a valid authenticated session exists.\n5. Only then allow navigation to protected application routes.\n\nIf authentication fails, **do not navigate to the dashboard**.\n\nDisplay a clear message such as:\n\n> \"No account found or incorrect email/password. Please sign up or check your credentials.\"\n\nDo not create an account automatically during login.\n\n### Existing user profile restoration\n\nAfter successful authentication:\n\n1. Get the authenticated Supabase `user.id`.\n2. Fetch the user\'s profile from the database using `user.id`.\n3. If the profile exists and onboarding is complete:\n\n   * Restore all saved information.\n   * Skip onboarding.\n   * Navigate directly to the dashboard.\n4. If the profile is missing/incomplete:\n\n   * Navigate to onboarding.\n   * Pre-fill any existing information.\n   * Save the completed profile using the same `user.id`.\n\nThe same user must always retrieve the same profile.\n\n### Protected routes\n\nMake sure the dashboard and ALL application features are protected at the routing level.\n\nFor every protected page/component:\n\n```text\nNo authenticated session\n        \342\206\223\nRedirect to Login\n```\n\n```text\nAuthenticated session\n        \342\206\223\nCheck profile\n        \342\206\223\nProfile incomplete \342\206\222 Onboarding\nProfile complete \342\206\222 Dashboard\n```\n\nUsers must not be able to bypass authentication by:\n\n* Typing a dashboard URL directly\n* Refreshing the page\n* Opening a protected route in a new tab\n* Manipulating frontend state\n* Returning to the app after logout\n\n### Logout\n\nWhen the user logs out:\n\n* Call Supabase sign-out.\n* Clear local authentication/profile state.\n* Invalidate the current session.\n* Redirect to the Intro/Login page.\n* Make sure protected pages cannot still be accessed using stale frontend state.\n\n### Session persistence\n\nFor users who have already logged in successfully:\n\n* Persist their Supabase session across page refreshes and browser/app restarts.\n* On application startup, check the current Supabase session.\n* Show a loading screen while checking the session.\n* Do NOT temporarily show the dashboard before authentication is verified.\n\n### Important security requirement\n\nDo NOT use a frontend variable such as:\n\n```js\nisLoggedIn = true\n```\n\nas the actual authentication mechanism.\n\nThe application must rely on the **real Supabase Auth session**.\n\nDo NOT treat:\n\n* Email entered in a form\n* User ID stored in localStorage\n* A manually created profile\n* Frontend state\n* Cached onboarding data\n\nas proof that the user is authenticated.\n\nOnly a valid Supabase Auth session should grant access to protected features.\n\n### Database security\n\nAlso inspect the Supabase database policies/RLS.\n\nUsers should only be able to read and modify their own profile data.\n\nThe relationship should be:\n\n`auth.users.id \342\206\222 profiles.user_id`\n\nand the database policies should enforce that users can only access their own records.\n\n### Test these cases\n\nAfter implementing the fix, test all of these scenarios:\n\n**Test 1 \342\200\224 New account**\n`Unknown email \342\206\222 Sign Up \342\206\222 Onboarding \342\206\222 Dashboard`\n\n**Test 2 \342\200\224 Existing account**\n`Existing email/password \342\206\222 Login \342\206\222 Existing profile restored \342\206\222 Dashboard`\n\n**Test 3 \342\200\224 Wrong password**\n`Existing email + wrong password \342\206\222 Login fails \342\206\222 Stay on Login`\n\n**Test 4 \342\200\224 Non-existing account**\n`Email that has never signed up \342\206\222 Login fails \342\206\222 Stay on Login`\n\n**Test 5 \342\200\224 Logout**\n`Dashboard \342\206\222 Logout \342\206\222 Login/Intro \342\206\222 Dashboard cannot be accessed`\n\n**Test 6 \342\200\224 Refresh**\n`Logged-in user \342\206\222 Refresh \342\206\222 Session restored \342\206\222 Dashboard`\n\n**Test 7 \342\200\224 Existing user with incomplete profile**\n`Login \342\206\222 Existing partial profile \342\206\222 Onboarding \342\206\222 Complete \342\206\222 Dashboard`\n\nPlease inspect the entire existing authentication, routing, Supabase configuration, profile database logic, RLS policies, and onboarding flow. Fix the underlying issue instead of adding a UI-only workaround.\n\nDo not remove or break any existing application features."
    }
  }
