  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Supabase Initialization**\n\nI\'m currently digging into the initialization process of Supabase within `src/backend/supabase_service.ts`. My focus is on understanding how `supabase.auth` and the user accounts registry function, especially in the context of `signIn` and profile retrieval. I\'m starting by dissecting the initialization code to grasp the foundational setup.\n\n\n**Verifying Supabase Configuration**\n\nI\'m now investigating the configuration check using `SupabaseService.isConfigured()`. I\'ve confirmed it correctly flags placeholder URLs.  I am observing what happens when Supabase is *not* configured and how the authentication flow and user creation are affected. Specifically, how a non-existent user, such as one with the `usr_demo_101` ID, interacts with the system in this state.\n\n\n**Addressing Authentication Bypass**\n\nI\'ve uncovered a critical vulnerability: the system was blindly returning a `localUser` from `localStorage` without validating credentials or checking the accounts registry. This bypasses the intended authentication flow, even if Supabase is properly configured. If `isConfigured()` is false, there needs to be a local user accounts registry to fail attempts to login with non-existent accounts and incorrect passwords. I\'m now implementing the necessary checks to ensure only valid users gain access.\n\n\n**Refining Login Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating stricter checks for existing user logins. I\'ve implemented logic to *prevent* automatic account creation; accounts must already exist in the user registry or Supabase Auth. My code now explicitly calls `supabase.auth.signInWithPassword` when Supabase is configured, ensuring existing accounts are found by email. I\'m focusing on handling the return of any error or a null user, preventing unauthorized access by providing a clear error message in the AuthModal.\n\n\n**Confirming User Consistency**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on user ID consistency after login. My tests confirm that logging in after onboarding *must* return the same user ID, whether through Supabase or the local registry. This is crucial for retrieving the correct onboarding profile from either Supabase or local storage. I\'m focusing on ensuring the `signIn` function accurately matches the original user ID, specifically `\"usr_1720000000\"` or \"uuid-1234\", and not defaulting to any demo accounts, which were an earlier error.\n\n\n**Analyzing User Sign-Up**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the user sign-up flow. I\'m verifying the account creation process in Supabase (or the user registry, if Supabase is unavailable). I will examine the generation of valid Supabase sessions and profile checks for `hasCompleted = false`. I\'m going to track navigation to the Onboarding wizard, and I\'ll analyze how the user\'s data is saved to the `farmer_onboarding` table after onboarding completion, including the setting of `hasCompletedOnboarding` and the final navigation to the Dashboard.\n\n\n**Implementing Onboarding Profile Retrieval**\n\nI\'m now implementing the logic for retrieving user profiles after a user is authenticated. I\'m focusing on the `getOnboardingProfile(userId)` function and validating the profile from the Supabase DB or local storage. If a user has completed the onboarding, I\'ll restore state and navigate to the dashboard. If not, the user goes to the onboarding wizard. I\'m also planning error handling for missing profiles or incomplete data.\n\n**Handling Invalid User Login**\n\nI\'m focusing on the invalid user login flow. I\'m creating the flow `Intro -> Login -> Authentication Fails -> Stay on Login -> Show Error`. I\'m designing the display for error messages to show if the user does not exist or has incorrect credentials. The user will be required to stay in the Login modal and re-enter credentials or sign up. There will be no access to the Dashboard and no creation or login of a fake user.\n\n**Securing Session and Routing**\n\nI\'m strengthening the routes with robust session checks. I\'ll make sure `App.tsx` has a valid Supabase Auth session. I\'ll also ensure routes rely on session data, preventing unauthorized access by managing the routes correctly. The implementation will ensure only authenticated users can access protected parts of the app.\n\n\n**Validating Route Access**\n\nI\'m now implementing strict checks for user authentication and session validity upon page load and refresh. I\'m focusing on `App.tsx` and ensuring that the Dashboard or any protected component only renders when a valid Supabase session exists, with both a user ID and completed onboarding. I\'m verifying authentication status and fetching onboarding profiles based on session state, including secure sign-out and route access restrictions.\n\n\n**Verifying Placeholder URL**\n\nI\'m now investigating how the `isConfigured()` function within `SupabaseService` reacts in a runtime environment, especially when encountering placeholder URLs or the absence of a proper Supabase setup. I\'m focusing on the behavior of `meta.env?.VITE_SUPABASE_URL` in different scenarios to verify the function\'s expected output.\n\n\n**Designing Local Auth Fallback**\n\nI\'m now designing the local authentication fallback mechanism. My focus is on ensuring seamless operation with a local user accounts registry when Supabase is unavailable. I\'m building a robust `nutriharvest_users_registry` within `localStorage`. This registry will mirror Supabase\'s behavior, ensuring the same security rules apply. The goal is to provide a consistent experience, whether the system is connected to Supabase or operating locally.\n\n\n**Refining Account Creation**\n\nI\'m now refining the user account creation process, especially for scenarios when Supabase is unavailable. I\'m focusing on creating users, or blocking, based on the email within the local `nutriharvest_users_registry`. The logic will include an error check if the account already exists. When Supabase isn\'t configured, a user\'s local session will be saved to `localStorage`. I\'m verifying the account creation workflow and data persistence using `localStorage`.\n\n\n\n**Validating Fallback Authentication**\n\nI\'m now implementing the detailed fallback authentication using the `nutriharvest_users_registry`. I\'m verifying the exact error messages for invalid sign-in attempts, specifically when a user\'s email does not exist, or the password is incorrect. No account is automatically created on login, so users must sign up first. I\'m focusing on ensuring the proper `userId` is returned on successful login from the registry, guaranteeing data consistency.\n\n\n**Analyzing Profile Handling**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the `getOnboardingProfile(userId)` function in detail. I\'m focusing on how the system retrieves user profiles, both from Supabase and from local storage when Supabase is unavailable. My goal is to ensure data consistency. I\'ll normalize user IDs, query the Supabase `farmer_onboarding` table when available, and then fall back to local storage if needed. If Supabase is unavailable, I\'ll leverage local storage as the primary data source. I\'ll handle the absence of a profile gracefully by returning `hasCompleted: false`.\n\n\n**Implementing Profile Storage**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `setOnboardingProfile(userId, data)` function for storing user profile data. I\'m focusing on ensuring data persistence whether Supabase is available or not. In the local backup, I\'ll save the data to both `localStorage` under a specific key and to a `nutriharvest_onboarding_db` map. When Supabase is configured, I\'ll upsert the data to the `farmer_onboarding` table, along with the required fields, and the `profiles` table.\n\n\n"
