    thinking: "**Defining UserSession Structure**\n\nI\'ve been working on defining the `UserSession` structure. It encompasses user data like ID, email, and farmer name (optional), along with login and offline status, and the last sync timestamp. This structure is intended to capture all essential session information in one place.\n\n\n**Analyzing New User Flow**\n\nI\'m now deeply immersed in the new user flow requirements. I\'ve begun to break down each step, from the initial \"Intro\" to the final \"Dashboard\" phase. My focus is on ensuring a smooth transition between components, particularly within the `AuthModal` where the signup process is initiated. I am thinking carefully about error handling, such as duplicate email situations, and the successful user session setup after successful Supabase signup. The role of `onAuthSuccess` and onboarding completion status are clear.\n\n\n**Mapping User Journeys**\n\nI\'m now detailing user flows, specifically onboarding and existing user paths. The onboarding process involves a UI presenting the `FarmerProfileWizard`, data saving to the `farmer_onboarding` table, and navigating to the dashboard after profile updates. For existing users, I\'m defining the path from the intro to the dashboard. The `AuthModal` flow now includes login via SupabaseService, session state updates, and an `onAuthSuccess` hook to fetch and handle onboarding profile retrieval.\n\n\n**Handling Login Failures**\n\nI\'m now focusing on what happens when a user login fails, or when a user tries to login with credentials that do not exist. Specifically, when SupabaseService returns an error, this error needs to be caught in the `AuthModal`. I\'m working on how to properly display an error message to the user, and to ensure they remain on the login view. The login modal will show the appropriate error, and `setSession` will NOT be called, and the user won\'t navigate from that location.\n\n\n**Implementing Sign Out & Startup**\n\nI\'ve outlined the sign-out process, which now includes calling `SupabaseService.signOut()`, clearing session storage, updating the session state to `null`, and resetting the onboarding status. Additionally, I\'ve detailed the session persistence logic during page loads. It checks for an active session, retrieves the onboarding profile, and sets the app\'s state accordingly. If the user is authenticated, I\'ll direct them to the appropriate tab. I\'m ensuring a loading screen is shown while verifying authentication, preventing premature display of the dashboard.\n\n**Verifying Database & Policies**\n\nI\'m verifying the database and the RLS (Row Level Security) policies on the `farmer_onboarding` and `profiles` tables. The policies ensure that users can only interact with their own data. I will check the Supabase Service implementation, confirming that it has clean auth methods.\n\n**Refining Supabase Service**\n\nI\'m now refining the `SupabaseService` to seamlessly handle both real Supabase (with valid environment variables) and a standard fallback for local accounts when the environment is offline, which involves local storage with `nutriharvest_users_db` and `nutriharvest_active_session`.\n\n\n**Defining Local Fallback**\n\nI\'m working on the local fallback mechanism. I\'m storing user data, in the form of a stringified object map, within `nutriharvest_onboarding_db`. I\'m tracing the `signUp()` method within `SupabaseService` to handle local user registration when a Supabase backend isn\'t available, including creating a local user, storing local user data with an id, and returning the proper data to the UI. I\'ve considered that login should be validated in the same way.\n\n\n**Implementing Local Session Logic**\n\nI\'m now detailing the logic within `SupabaseService` for local session management. Specifically, I\'m focusing on user creation and session persistence when a Supabase backend is unavailable. I\'m updating `signUp()` to handle local user registration, storing the new user\'s information and setting up the local session. I\'ve considered that the `login()` and `signOut()` methods should be validated in the same way.\n\n\n**Analyzing SignIn Function**\n\nI\'m now tracing the `signIn()` method within `SupabaseService`. I\'m focusing on the local fallback scenario when a Supabase backend isn\'t available. I\'ve begun reviewing the process, which involves checking the local `nutriharvest_users_db` for matching credentials. This includes retrieving stored users, verifying the email and password against the local registry, and returning a session object if a match is found. The error handling for invalid credentials is also checked.\n\n\n**Validating Local Credential**\n\nI\'m now implementing the validation of local credentials for the `signIn()` function. I\'ve been reviewing the code that checks the local `nutriharvest_users_db` database for matching credentials. This process involves retrieving stored users and verifying the email and password against the local registry, returning a session object upon a match. I have been paying attention to the error handling for invalid credentials.\n\n\n**Refining Login Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on error management for local user logins. I\'ve confirmed that the system returns specific errors: \"No account found\" and \"Incorrect password\" for unregistered or incorrect credentials, respectively. These checks are applied consistently in both the live Supabase and local fallback modes. I\'m focusing on ensuring these errors are properly displayed to the user in the login flow. I\'m also ensuring that no local account is inadvertently created during the login process. Finally, I\'m tracing `getSession()`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Session Persistence**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the `getSession()` function and the `signOut()` function. I\'m focusing on retrieving the user\'s data and verifying the session data in both Supabase and local modes. I\'m carefully reviewing the logic for removing the active session from local storage during sign-out, ensuring a clean session reset, and preventing stale data. I\'m also examining `getOnboardingProfile()` for fetching farmer and farm profile.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Profile Loading**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the logic for profile loading. I\'m focusing on the efficiency of retrieving the `farmer` and `farm` profiles. I am assessing the order of operations: first checking the local DB map, and then querying the Supabase database if configured. I have been paying close attention to error handling in case there are parsing issues within local storage. I\'m ensuring both processes are handled correctly.\n\n\n**Defining Profile Loading**\n\nI\'m now detailing the profile data fetching. I\'m focused on populating the profile objects, based on data available, prioritizing values from the database, followed by local fallback values. I\'ve designed a clear structure for `FarmerProfile` and `FarmProfile`. I\'ve been attentive to the data structure and default values, using a ternary operator to define defaults. The goal is complete and accurate profiles for both farmers and farms.\n\n\n\n**Refining Profile Fallback**\n\nI\'m now refining the local fallback process for farmer and farm profiles. I\'m focusing on ensuring data consistency and completeness when retrieving from local storage. I\'m validating the structure, ensuring default values are set for any missing data within both `farmer` and `farm` objects, specifically within the `soil` property. I\'m ensuring there are no errors when parsing local storage, and that the `cropHistory` field is an array. I\'m prioritizing user experience with a well-formed profile.\n\n\n**Validating Save Operations**\n\nI\'m now validating the `saveOnboardingProfile()` operation, focusing on data consistency, especially between local storage and Supabase. I\'m verifying local storage updates, including the use of `nutriharvest_onboarding_db`. I\'m also ensuring that local profile data is appropriately persisted. I will work through the Supabase save, including `farmer` and `farm` profiles.\n\nI\'ve also validated that the process will return a success state if the Supabase backend is down.\n\n\n**Validating Farm Profile Sync**\n\nI\'m now validating the farm profile sync and ensuring Supabase interaction is consistent. I\'ve focused on ensuring the `upsert` operation for the `farmer_onboarding` table properly updates the farm data. I\'m prioritizing data integrity in both local and Supabase modes. I\'m focusing on handling potential errors from the `upsert` and ensuring appropriate fallback actions.\n\n\n**Verifying Profile Saving**\n\nI\'m now tracing the `saveOnboardingProfile()` function and `AuthModal.tsx` interactions. I\'m carefully reviewing the logic to ensure that both the `farmer` and `farm` profiles are being saved correctly, and that local fallback is implemented when necessary. I\'m verifying the Supabase interaction, the `upsert` and the success state, and the clean hand-off with the local process.\n\n\n**Refining UI Interaction**\n\nI\'m now refining the UI interaction, based on successful and unsuccessful sign-in events. Specifically, after sign-up, the UI displays a success message, calls `onAuthSuccess`, and triggers a short delay before closing. For login, I\'m verifying the handling of successful login scenarios and error messages during failed login attempts. I\'m ensuring both processes are handled correctly and show the appropriate UI feedback.\n\n\n**Analyzing UI Updates**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the UI updates within `App.tsx` and the `AuthModal` flow, specifically related to sign-up and sign-in success and failure. After a failed sign-in, I\'ve confirmed the error message persists, and the modal remains open with no session set. For the happy path, I am tracing the success message display, including the `onAuthSuccess` call in `App.tsx` and handling of the session within the `App` component.\n\n\n**Validating Startup Flow**\n\nI\'m now validating the startup flow to ensure a seamless experience. When the app initializes, I\'m checking for an existing user session. If a session exists, the app fetches the onboarding profile, sets the farmer and farm data, and determines whether to direct the user to the dashboard or profile. I\'ve also implemented error handling. If no session exists, the app clears the onboarding data.\n\n\n**Refining Auth State Handling**\n\nI\'m now refining the auth state handling within `onAuthStateChange`. I\'m verifying the updates to the session state when authentication changes. I\'m focusing on the logic to retrieve the onboarding profile and update the app\'s state with farmer and farm data. I\'m checking the correct tab is selected based on onboarding status. Specifically, I\'m ensuring there are no errors when a user logs in, and the correct tab displays.\n\n\n"
