  planner_response {
    response: "I have resolved the authentication and security issues, enforcing a strict Supabase Auth flow and user profile management:\n\n- **Strict User Authentication & Credentials Verification**:\n  - Removed all hardcoded demo fallbacks and local session bypasses.\n  - Implemented exact user matching for login and sign-up. Non-existing user accounts or invalid passwords are strictly denied access with the error message: *\"No account found or incorrect email/password. Please sign up or check your credentials.\"*\n\n- **Profile & Onboarding Restoration**:\n  - Existing users logging in are authenticated via Supabase Auth and their onboarding profile is automatically retrieved using their specific `userId` (`auth.users.id \342\206\222 farmer_onboarding.user_id`).\n  - Restored profile data directly opens the Executive Dashboard without re-prompting for onboarding inputs.\n\n- **Route Protection & Flow Enforcement**:\n  - **New User**: `Intro \342\206\222 Sign Up \342\206\222 Account Created \342\206\222 Guided Onboarding \342\206\222 Save Profile \342\206\222 Dashboard`\n  - **Existing User**: `Intro \342\206\222 Login \342\206\222 Authenticate \342\206\222 Restore Profile \342\206\222 Dashboard`\n  - **Unauthenticated/Invalid User**: `Intro \342\206\222 Login \342\206\222 Error Displayed \342\206\222 Remain on Login`\n  - **Session Verification**: Page refreshes check active Supabase Auth sessions before rendering protected features. Logging out terminates the active session and returns the app to the Landing Page.\n\n- **Database Security & RLS**:\n  - Created `supabase_schema.sql` detailing the PostgreSQL schema for `profiles` and `farmer_onboarding` with Row Level Security (RLS) policies enforcing `auth.uid() = user_id`."
    thinking: "**Verifying Data Integrity**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the `metadata.json` file is both clean and accurate, representing a solid foundation. Now, I\'m performing a final cross-check. I\'m reviewing all the changes against the user requirements, particularly focusing on how strict user authentication is implemented with Supabase Auth as the source of truth.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have resolved the authentication and security issues, enforcing a strict Supabase Auth flow and user profile management:\n\n- **Strict User Authentication & Credentials Verification**:\n  - Removed all hardcoded demo fallbacks and local session bypasses.\n  - Implemented exact user matching for login and sign-up. Non-existing user accounts or invalid passwords are strictly denied access with the error message: *\"No account found or incorrect email/password. Please sign up or check your credentials.\"*\n\n- **Profile & Onboarding Restoration**:\n  - Existing users logging in are authenticated via Supabase Auth and their onboarding profile is automatically retrieved using their specific `userId` (`auth.users.id \342\206\222 farmer_onboarding.user_id`).\n  - Restored profile data directly opens the Executive Dashboard without re-prompting for onboarding inputs.\n\n- **Route Protection & Flow Enforcement**:\n  - **New User**: `Intro \342\206\222 Sign Up \342\206\222 Account Created \342\206\222 Guided Onboarding \342\206\222 Save Profile \342\206\222 Dashboard`\n  - **Existing User**: `Intro \342\206\222 Login \342\206\222 Authenticate \342\206\222 Restore Profile \342\206\222 Dashboard`\n  - **Unauthenticated/Invalid User**: `Intro \342\206\222 Login \342\206\222 Error Displayed \342\206\222 Remain on Login`\n  - **Session Verification**: Page refreshes check active Supabase Auth sessions before rendering protected features. Logging out terminates the active session and returns the app to the Landing Page.\n\n- **Database Security & RLS**:\n  - Created `supabase_schema.sql` detailing the PostgreSQL schema for `profiles` and `farmer_onboarding` with Row Level Security (RLS) policies enforcing `auth.uid() = user_id`."
