    thinking: "**Defining the Core Objective**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the user\'s detailed specifications. My primary focus is establishing the core objective: a robust agricultural platform. It must be a decision-support and farm-progress tracking system, underpinned by a strict \"NO FAKE DATA POLICY\". I am prioritizing a platform that delivers real-world value and trustworthy information for the user\'s domain.\n\n\n**Clarifying Data Integrity**\n\nI\'m now concretizing the data integrity mandates. My core emphasis centers around a strict \"NO FAKE DATA POLICY.\" I will always prioritize verified sources: user input, approved datasets, reliable ML models, and live APIs. If data is missing, I\'ll flag an explicit \"Data Unavailable\" prompt. All modules must be driven by user-specific farm and farmer profiles.\n\n\n**Focusing on User-Specific Needs**\n\nI\'ve just refined the features to ensure calculations are personalized, avoiding generic data. I\'m focusing now on integrating user-specific nutritional needs and linking these to current crop production. I\'ll translate gaps into concrete crop recommendations. I also want to provide explainable reasoning for each crop recommendation and to incorporate real machine learning for yield predictions and tracking.\n\n\n**Integrating Real-time Data Streams**\n\nI\'m currently incorporating live data streams for irrigation recommendations. I\'m focusing on calculating daily water demand using evapotranspiration, rainfall forecasts, and soil moisture estimates. I\'ll translate this into specific irrigation guidance and integrate it with a new daily farm progress tracking module. This includes a visual timeline of activities and a comparison of predicted yields with actuals.\n\n\n"
