  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Connections & Features**\n\nI\'m now diving into the component connections. I\'ve begun mapping out how each part integrates and what new features we must integrate. Specifically, I am focusing on the \"No Fake Data Policy\" and transparency for the data source. I think \"data badges\" would be appropriate for display of user data and other key metrics. I will need to refine the design later.\n\n\n**Defining Data Inputs**\n\nI\'ve been mapping out data inputs, focusing on categories: Live API feeds, verified datasets, ML model predictions, and calculated values. I\'m prioritizing how to handle missing data with explicit \"Data Unavailable\" states and user prompts. Specifically, I\'m thinking about an \"action required\" notification for missing farm profile details.\n\nI\'m now diving into the component connections. I\'ve begun mapping out how each part integrates and what new features we must integrate. Specifically, I am focusing on the \"No Fake Data Policy\" and transparency for the data source. I think \"data badges\" would be appropriate for display of user data and other key metrics. I will need to refine the design later.\n\n\n**Refining Crop Recommendation System**\n\nI\'m now integrating the crop recommendation system with the UI, mapping required household nutrition to current production yield and identifying nutritional gaps. I\'m focusing on the `CropPlanningAgent.ts` and `CropPlanCard.tsx` files. I am working to rank candidate crops based on user inputs. The goal is to provide explicit reasons for each crop recommendation, itemizing factors like soil match and nutritional benefits. I am also working on yield prediction and tracking.\n\n\n**Tracking Farm Progress**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the \"FarmProgressTracker\" component, developing an interactive activity log and timeline. This will record daily and periodic details like growth stages, irrigation, rainfall, fertilizer use, and pest observations. I\'m focusing on the visual dashboard to show the status of each crop, and how to track and persist data in Supabase/LocalStorage linked to the user\'s ID. I\'m also planning to incorporate Live Irrigation Recommendations using Open-Meteo data for precise water advice.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 439670120
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
