steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1786466246
      nanos: 623451262
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Make ONLY the following changes to the existing application. Do not modify or remove unrelated features.\n\n### 1. Fix the Nutrition Calculation\n\nThe nutrition section must be based on **what the farmer is actually planting/growing**, not random or generic numbers.\n\nThe calculation should work like this:\n\n**Farmer\'s crop \342\206\222 Crop quantity/yield \342\206\222 Verified nutrition data \342\206\222 Total nutrition produced \342\206\222 Household nutrition coverage**\n\nFor example, if the farmer is growing wheat, the system should:\n\n1. Identify that the farmer is growing wheat.\n2. Get the farmer\'s farm area and expected/actual yield.\n3. Use a verified nutrition dataset containing the nutritional composition of wheat.\n4. Calculate the actual amount of nutrients provided by the farmer\'s production.\n5. Compare those nutrients with the household\'s nutritional requirements.\n6. Show exactly how much of each nutrient is covered.\n\nFor example, the UI should show something like:\n\n```text\nCrop: Wheat\nProduction: 500 kg\n\nProtein produced: [calculated from real data]\nCalories produced: [calculated from real data]\nIron produced: [calculated from real data]\nCalcium produced: [calculated from real data]\n\nHousehold requirement:\nProtein: [calculated requirement]\n\nCoverage:\nProtein: XX%\nIron: XX%\nCalcium: XX%\n```\n\n**Do NOT use random, hardcoded, placeholder, or made-up nutrition values.**\n\nEvery nutrition number must be calculated from:\n\n* The crop the farmer is growing\n* The quantity/yield of that crop\n* A real/verified nutritional dataset\n* The household information already provided by the farmer\n\nIf a verified nutrition dataset is not currently connected, **do not generate fake numbers**. Clearly indicate that the nutrition calculation requires a verified dataset.\n\n### 2. Use Actual vs Predicted Yield Correctly\n\nIf the farmer has not harvested yet, use the **predicted yield** and clearly label the nutrition result as:\n\n> \"Estimated nutrition based on predicted yield.\"\n\nOnce the farmer enters their actual harvested yield, recalculate the nutrition using the **actual yield** and label it:\n\n> \"Nutrition based on actual recorded yield.\"\n\nDo not mix predicted and actual values.\n\n### 3. Delete Journal Entries\n\nAdd a **Delete** button to every journal entry.\n\nWhen the farmer deletes an entry:\n\n* Ask for confirmation.\n* Delete the record from the database.\n* Remove it from the UI.\n* Do not just hide it locally.\n\n### 4. Delete Yield History\n\nAdd a **Delete** button to every yield history record.\n\nWhen deleted:\n\n* Ask for confirmation.\n* Delete the record from the database.\n* Remove it from the UI.\n* Recalculate any statistics/charts that depend on that record.\n* Update any calculations that use that yield.\n\n### 5. Add Refresh Buttons\n\nAdd a **Refresh** button for all dynamically generated, calculated, or externally retrieved data.\n\nThis should include, where applicable:\n\n* Nutrition calculations\n* Crop recommendations\n* Yield predictions\n* Weather data\n* Mandi prices\n* Farm progress\n* Dashboard statistics\n\nThe Refresh button must actually fetch/recalculate the data again.\n\nShow a loading state while refreshing and display the latest update time when appropriate.\n\nDo not simply reload the entire page.\n\n### 6. Remove \"Load Data\" / Demo Data\n\nCompletely remove the **\"Load Data\", \"Load Demo Data\", \"Load Sample Data\"** or similar functionality from the application.\n\nDo not populate the application with fake/sample farmer data.\n\nIf there is no real data available, show an appropriate empty state such as:\n\n> \"No data available yet. Add your farm and crop information to get started.\"\n\nDo NOT replace missing data with random or sample values.\n\n### Final Requirement\n\nAudit these specific areas and make sure there are **NO random or fabricated numbers** being used for nutrition, yield, or generated statistics.\n\nEvery value must come from:\n\n**Farmer input + real database data + verified dataset + actual API data + legitimate calculations/ML predictions.**\n\nDo not change any other existing functionality."
    items {
      text: "Make ONLY the following changes to the existing application. Do not modify or remove unrelated features.\n\n### 1. Fix the Nutrition Calculation\n\nThe nutrition section must be based on **what the farmer is actually planting/growing**, not random or generic numbers.\n\nThe calculation should work like this:\n\n**Farmer\'s crop \342\206\222 Crop quantity/yield \342\206\222 Verified nutrition data \342\206\222 Total nutrition produced \342\206\222 Household nutrition coverage**\n\nFor example, if the farmer is growing wheat, the system should:\n\n1. Identify that the farmer is growing wheat.\n2. Get the farmer\'s farm area and expected/actual yield.\n3. Use a verified nutrition dataset containing the nutritional composition of wheat.\n4. Calculate the actual amount of nutrients provided by the farmer\'s production.\n5. Compare those nutrients with the household\'s nutritional requirements.\n6. Show exactly how much of each nutrient is covered.\n\nFor example, the UI should show something like:\n\n```text\nCrop: Wheat\nProduction: 500 kg\n\nProtein produced: [calculated from real data]\nCalories produced: [calculated from real data]\nIron produced: [calculated from real data]\nCalcium produced: [calculated from real data]\n\nHousehold requirement:\nProtein: [calculated requirement]\n\nCoverage:\nProtein: XX%\nIron: XX%\nCalcium: XX%\n```\n\n**Do NOT use random, hardcoded, placeholder, or made-up nutrition values.**\n\nEvery nutrition number must be calculated from:\n\n* The crop the farmer is growing\n* The quantity/yield of that crop\n* A real/verified nutritional dataset\n* The household information already provided by the farmer\n\nIf a verified nutrition dataset is not currently connected, **do not generate fake numbers**. Clearly indicate that the nutrition calculation requires a verified dataset.\n\n### 2. Use Actual vs Predicted Yield Correctly\n\nIf the farmer has not harvested yet, use the **predicted yield** and clearly label the nutrition result as:\n\n> \"Estimated nutrition based on predicted yield.\"\n\nOnce the farmer enters their actual harvested yield, recalculate the nutrition using the **actual yield** and label it:\n\n> \"Nutrition based on actual recorded yield.\"\n\nDo not mix predicted and actual values.\n\n### 3. Delete Journal Entries\n\nAdd a **Delete** button to every journal entry.\n\nWhen the farmer deletes an entry:\n\n* Ask for confirmation.\n* Delete the record from the database.\n* Remove it from the UI.\n* Do not just hide it locally.\n\n### 4. Delete Yield History\n\nAdd a **Delete** button to every yield history record.\n\nWhen deleted:\n\n* Ask for confirmation.\n* Delete the record from the database.\n* Remove it from the UI.\n* Recalculate any statistics/charts that depend on that record.\n* Update any calculations that use that yield.\n\n### 5. Add Refresh Buttons\n\nAdd a **Refresh** button for all dynamically generated, calculated, or externally retrieved data.\n\nThis should include, where applicable:\n\n* Nutrition calculations\n* Crop recommendations\n* Yield predictions\n* Weather data\n* Mandi prices\n* Farm progress\n* Dashboard statistics\n\nThe Refresh button must actually fetch/recalculate the data again.\n\nShow a loading state while refreshing and display the latest update time when appropriate.\n\nDo not simply reload the entire page.\n\n### 6. Remove \"Load Data\" / Demo Data\n\nCompletely remove the **\"Load Data\", \"Load Demo Data\", \"Load Sample Data\"** or similar functionality from the application.\n\nDo not populate the application with fake/sample farmer data.\n\nIf there is no real data available, show an appropriate empty state such as:\n\n> \"No data available yet. Add your farm and crop information to get started.\"\n\nDo NOT replace missing data with random or sample values.\n\n### Final Requirement\n\nAudit these specific areas and make sure there are **NO random or fabricated numbers** being used for nutrition, yield, or generated statistics.\n\nEvery value must come from:\n\n**Farmer input + real database data + verified dataset + actual API data + legitimate calculations/ML predictions.**\n\nDo not change any other existing functionality."
