  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Conditional Logic**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `App.tsx` file, specifically the handling of default profiles. The core of the update involves ensuring that `farmer` and `farm` do *not* default to demo profiles when no user is logged in *or* when no onboarding profile is saved in local storage. I\'m double-checking the conditions to ensure the intended behavior when no onboarding profile exists.\n\n\n**Verifying Initial State**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that if `farmer` and `farm` are null (no user, no onboarding data), we strictly adhere to requirement 6. The UI should display the empty state: \"No data available yet. Add your farm and crop information to get started.\" I\'m verifying this by examining how the UI handles null `farmer` and `farm` values across different views like the Dashboard and Nutrition. I\'m also ensuring the absence of any \"Load Data\" functionality, as per the spec.\n\n\n**Designing Nutrition Calculation**\n\nI\'m now diving into requirements 1 and 2, focusing on nutrition calculation logic and yield source determination. I\'m prioritizing establishing how the active crop and production are identified. I\'m investigating how the system checks for `actual harvest yield(s)` within `YieldTrackingAgent.getRecordsForUser(userId)`. My immediate focus is on ensuring the correct yield source (ACTUAL) and yield label are set when `actualRecords` contain harvest data.\n\n\n**Calculating Yield and Nutrition**\n\nI\'m now determining yield sources and building the nutrition calculations based on existing data. When `YieldTrackingAgent` lacks actual yield data, I\'m sourcing yield from the planned crops, using the `totalExpectedYieldKg` of allocated candidates, and setting a \"Predicted Yield\" badge and the corresponding label. I\'m prioritizing establishing how the crop-specific nutritional information is looked up in the nutrition dataset for each crop.\n\n\n**Calculating Nutrient Outputs**\n\nI\'m now implementing the nutrition calculations. I\'m focusing on the logic for computing the nutrient values produced by each crop, leveraging a multiplier based on quantity in kilograms. This involves multiplying per-100g values by the quantity. I am handling instances when a crop\'s nutrition data isn\'t in the verified dataset by recording that the data is missing. Finally, I\'m summing total nutrients produced across all crops. I\'m moving on to household requirement calculation.\n\n\n**Determining Coverage Percentages**\n\nI\'m now calculating coverage percentages for the UI, focusing on the method: `Math.min(100, Math.round((totalProduced / monthlyTarget) * 100))`. I\'m integrating this calculation within `NutritionDashboard.tsx` and `ExecutiveDashboard.tsx` to display nutrient coverage against household targets. I\'m focusing on ensuring accurate representation of both actual and estimated yield sources, including correct display of associated badges and banners.\n\n\n**Refactoring Nutrition Calculations**\n\nI\'m now determining whether to update `NutritionAgent` or create `calculateCropNutritionFromYield` to centralize nutrition logic. I\'m focusing on ensuring deterministic crop name resolution against `IFCT2017_CROP_NUTRITION` by testing various input formats (e.g., \"Wheat\", \"WHEAT\", \"Paddy / Rice\") to match the correct standard. I\'m looking for consistency in matching existing crops.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 985939200
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
