  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Yield Tracking**\n\nI\'m currently integrating a callback function, tentatively named `onRecordChange` or `onYieldUpdated`, into the `YieldTrackingModal.tsx` component. My goal is to trigger this function whenever a user modifies a yield record, either by adding or deleting it. For deletion, I\'m working on implementing the record deletion within the modal.\n\n\n**Implementing Delete Confirmation**\n\nI\'ve added the crucial \"Delete\" button within the record header for the modal, along with associated logic. Upon confirmation, the targeted record is deleted, the data is reloaded, and I\'ve also implemented the `onYieldUpdated()` callback. This should effectively trigger recalculations and nutrition adjustments as expected, since `recalculateAgents()` will check for yield records and then use the actual harvest yield.\n\n\n**Adding Refresh Buttons**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the refresh functionality outlined in Requirement 5. Currently, I\'m working on adding refresh buttons to dynamically generated data components. I\'m starting with the `ExecutiveDashboard.tsx` component, where I\'ll introduce a refresh button within the header. My aim is to make it fetch and recalculate dashboard statistics and overall farm plan data. I plan to incorporate a loading state during the refresh and display the last updated time.\n\n\n**Adding Refresh Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating refresh buttons across multiple components to enhance data accuracy and user experience. Specifically, I\'m working on the NutritionDashboard, implementing a button that triggers recalculation of nutrition data, yields, and coverage using the IFCT 2017 dataset. This refresh action will be accompanied by a loading spinner and a timestamp to indicate when the data was last updated. I\'m taking a similar approach for the CropPlanCard, to re-evaluate yield predictions based on the farm profile, and also for the ClimateWidget, to refresh weather data from the Open-Meteo API. I\'m focusing on ensuring consistent loading states and timestamp updates across all these components.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 113633696
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
