  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Onboarding Logic**\n\nOkay, I\'ve zeroed in on the `App.tsx` file. I\'m focusing on the user sign-up and sign-in flow. It appears that if a new user hasn\'t created a farm profile, the `farmer` and `farm` data is uninitialized or requires onboarding. The key seems to be the `hasCompletedOnboarding` flag, which changes state after profile creation.\n\n\n**Investigating Empty States**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implications of unpopulated `farm` or `farmer` data, particularly missing land size or household details. I\'ve found the correct empty state message: \"No data available yet. Add your farm and crop information to get started.\" I\'m also removing demo scenarios to load states from `localStorage` or `Supabase`. Finally, I\'m tracing `recalculateAgents` to see how it can address requirements one and two, related to household RDA targets and agent recalculation.\n\n\n**Exploring Agent Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the agents. First, I compute the household\'s monthly RDA targets based on age groups. Then, I generate crop candidates and yield predictions. I\'m also fetching hyperlocal weather data and mandi prices for the farm\'s state and primary crop. Finally, I\'m working on forecasting prices.\n\n\n**Evaluating Yield Source**\n\nI\'m now determining the yield source. I\'m prioritizing actual recorded yield data from the `YieldTrackingAgent` if it exists. Otherwise, I\'m using predicted yield data from candidate or planned crops. I\'ve also implemented a logic to aggregate the actual yield data for each crop, enabling a comprehensive comparison between the actual and predicted yields. This is crucial for accurate planning.\n\n\n**Calculating Nutrition Achieved**\n\nI\'m now calculating the nutrition achieved using the `NutritionAgent`. I\'m using a `cropYieldMap` to track total expected yields, and identifying the active crops\' yield source (PREDICTED or ACTUAL). Next, I calculate and set the nutrition coverage and source information, clearly labeling the yield source. Finally, I\'m setting a primary crop as a starting point.\n\n\n**Summarizing Farm Plan**\n\nI\'ve just implemented the `OptimizationAgent` to allocate harvests based on the primary crop, farmer details, prices, and forecasts, setting the harvest allocation. I\'m also structuring the farm plan, including key data like farmer name, location, land area, crops, yield source, nutrition coverage, and weather alerts. Finally, I\'m generating an explanation using Gemini, and updating the last refreshed time.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 698906225
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
