  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Nutritional Data**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `IFCT2017_CROP_NUTRITION` data within `src/data/ifct2017_nutrition.ts`. I\'ve identified the following crops: RICE, WHEAT, BAJRA, JOWAR, MAIZE, CHICKPEA, PIGEON_PEA, LENTIL, MOONG_BEAN, GROUNDNUT, and MUSTARD. I\'m noting these as a key part of the current nutritional data under consideration.\n\n\n**Expanding Crop List**\n\nI\'ve expanded the identified crop list to include POTATO, TOMATO, ONION, SPINACH, OKRA, and BRINJAL. I\'m also adding a helper function, `getCropNutritionInfo`, to `ifct2017_nutrition.ts`. This function will retrieve nutritional information based on a given crop key, handling case-insensitive matches and synonyms for robustness, such as \'corn\' and \'maize\'.\n\n\n**Refining Crop Matching Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the crop matching logic within `getCropNutritionInfo`. I\'ve added robust handling for various synonyms and local names. For example, \'chana\', \'bengal gram\', and \'chickpea\' are now correctly linked. The same level of detail has been implemented for PIGEON_PEA, LENTIL, MOONG_BEAN, GROUNDNUT, MUSTARD, POTATO, TOMATO, ONION, and SPINACH. I\'ve also integrated synonyms and regional names for OKRA.\n\n\n**Validating Data Mapping**\n\nI\'m verifying that every crop input, or generated by a candidate model, directly maps to its official ICMR-NIN IFCT 2017 composition entry. The matching function is implemented to ensure data accuracy. I\'ve integrated a check to handle missing dataset entries, providing a clear message to the user when data isn\'t available, per the requirement. I\'m now reviewing `NutritionDashboardProps` and `NutritionDashboard.tsx` to understand the data rendering process.\n\n\n**Visualizing Data Sources**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the yield source (`ACTUAL` or `PREDICTED`) is displayed within the `NutritionDashboard.tsx` component. I\'m implementing a source badge, using green for actual and amber for predicted yields, along with a corresponding message. I\'m also planning the detailed crop-by-crop nutrient production table, including crop name, quantity, yield status (actual vs. predicted), and specific nutrient breakdowns from the IFCT 2017 data.\n\n\n**Implementing Dashboard Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now integrating several enhancements to both `ExecutiveDashboard.tsx` and `CropPlanCard.tsx`. I\'ve added the refresh button with its spinning icon and the last updated timestamp. I\'m also ensuring the yield source badge is displayed correctly, indicating whether the nutrition data is based on actual or predicted yields. Finally, I\'m implementing the empty state message to display when no farm profile or data is available.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 611272780
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
