  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the updates to ensure complete data integrity, exact crop-based nutrition calculations, and explicit distinction between actual recorded yields and predicted yield estimates.\n\n### Key Enhancements Implemented:\n\n1. **Crop-to-Nutrition Calculation Pipeline**\n   - **Farmer Crop Selection**: Calculates total nutritional yield based strictly on crops actively planted or harvested on the farmer\'s land.\n   - **IFCT 2017 Verified Data Matching**: Utilized `getCropNutritionInfo` to resolve crop names and aliases against the official ICMR-NIN Indian Food Composition Tables 2017 dataset.\n   - **Household Requirement Comparison**: Compares total nutrient output against the household\'s exact RDA requirements (computed from household demographic age group counts).\n   - **Itemized Crop Breakdown**: Added an itemized table displaying exact nutrient outputs (Protein, Iron, Calcium, Vitamins, Fiber, Calories) for each planted crop.\n\n2. **Yield Provenance (Actual vs. Predicted)**\n   - Added a **Yield Source Banner** at the top of the Nutrition Dashboard.\n   - **Actual Yield Mode**: Automatically activates when the farmer logs actual harvest records in the *Harvest & Actual Yields* manager. Clearly labels outputs as *\"Nutrition calculated based on actual recorded yield from post-harvest logs\"*.\n   - **Predicted Yield Mode**: Used when no post-harvest logs exist yet, clearly labeling outputs as *\"Estimated nutrition based on predicted yield from ML models\"*.\n\n3. **Data Refresh & Management**\n   - **Manual Refresh Controls**: Added refresh buttons with timestamp indicators across all agent modules (*Dashboard, Nutrition, Crop Plan, Farm Journal, Harvest Yields, Climate Alerts, Mandi Prices*).\n   - **Record Deletion**: Enabled deletion for individual post-harvest yield logs and daily farm journal entries, triggering immediate recalculation across all AI agents.\n   - **Removal of Demo Data**: Cleaned up demo data banners and demo loading controls so the application operates strictly on user-managed profile data."
    thinking: "**Reviewing User Requirements**\n\nI\'ve successfully compiled the applet without any errors. Now, I\'m meticulously reviewing all user requests, focusing on requirement fulfillment. I\'m prioritizing the fix for the nutrition calculation, ensuring accuracy based on the farmer\'s input. The goal is to verify all requirements are addressed completely.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the updates to ensure complete data integrity, exact crop-based nutrition calculations, and explicit distinction between actual recorded yields and predicted yield estimates.\n\n### Key Enhancements Implemented:\n\n1. **Crop-to-Nutrition Calculation Pipeline**\n   - **Farmer Crop Selection**: Calculates total nutritional yield based strictly on crops actively planted or harvested on the farmer\'s land.\n   - **IFCT 2017 Verified Data Matching**: Utilized `getCropNutritionInfo` to resolve crop names and aliases against the official ICMR-NIN Indian Food Composition Tables 2017 dataset.\n   - **Household Requirement Comparison**: Compares total nutrient output against the household\'s exact RDA requirements (computed from household demographic age group counts).\n   - **Itemized Crop Breakdown**: Added an itemized table displaying exact nutrient outputs (Protein, Iron, Calcium, Vitamins, Fiber, Calories) for each planted crop.\n\n2. **Yield Provenance (Actual vs. Predicted)**\n   - Added a **Yield Source Banner** at the top of the Nutrition Dashboard.\n   - **Actual Yield Mode**: Automatically activates when the farmer logs actual harvest records in the *Harvest & Actual Yields* manager. Clearly labels outputs as *\"Nutrition calculated based on actual recorded yield from post-harvest logs\"*.\n   - **Predicted Yield Mode**: Used when no post-harvest logs exist yet, clearly labeling outputs as *\"Estimated nutrition based on predicted yield from ML models\"*.\n\n3. **Data Refresh & Management**\n   - **Manual Refresh Controls**: Added refresh buttons with timestamp indicators across all agent modules (*Dashboard, Nutrition, Crop Plan, Farm Journal, Harvest Yields, Climate Alerts, Mandi Prices*).\n   - **Record Deletion**: Enabled deletion for individual post-harvest yield logs and daily farm journal entries, triggering immediate recalculation across all AI agents.\n   - **Removal of Demo Data**: Cleaned up demo data banners and demo loading controls so the application operates strictly on user-managed profile data."
