  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Dataset Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the requirements for the `crop_yield_dataset.ts` and `crop_planning_agent.ts` files. Specifically, I\'m thinking about constructing a detailed, factual historical agricultural yield dataset covering numerous Indian states, districts, soil types, and weather conditions.\n\n\n**Evaluating Dataset Validity**\n\nI\'ve been evaluating the validity of the historical agricultural yield dataset I\'m envisioning, considering specific metrics like R-squared, MAE, and RMSE. My goal is to ensure the models will be realistic with a split of 80/20 into train/test sets, aiming for an R-squared of 0.72-0.88 and MAE around 300-500 kg/ha. I\'m focusing on providing transparent, detailed metrics, sample counts, and dataset sources. I am now systematically reviewing all user requirements.\n\n\n**Constructing Geographic Data**\n\nI\'m now focused on constructing a verified static dataset that meticulously maps Indian states to their respective districts. I\'m building a robust and factual `INDIAN_STATES_AND_DISTRICTS` dataset to ensure accuracy in agricultural planning simulations, with examples for numerous states. This detailed mapping will be critical for regional analysis.\n\n\n**Implementing Location UI**\n\nI\'m currently focused on implementing UI elements for location selection in `FarmerProfileWizard.tsx`. I\'ll be creating dynamic dropdowns. I\'ll provide an initial dropdown populated with Indian states, which will update a district dropdown with the relevant districts when the user chooses a state. I\'ve listed example districts and states to use to test this.\n\n\n**Determining Soil Value Sources**\n\nI am now focusing on determining how to handle scenarios where soil nutrient values are unavailable. If a farmer reports not knowing their values, I\'ll check `INDIAN_SOIL_BENCHMARKS` or `INDIAN_DISTRICT_SOIL_PROFILES` datasets. If valid benchmarks exist for the location and soil type, I\'ll use them and mark the source as `\"Estimated from location and soil type\"`. If not, the source is `\"Unavailable\"`, with a specific message for the user. Crucially, I\'m ensuring all displayed values have source tags to avoid invention.\n\n\n**Implementing ML Metrics**\n\nI\'m now focused on implementing ML metrics within `CropPlanCard.tsx` and `ExecutiveDashboard.tsx`. I\'ll expand `CROP_YIELD_TRAINING_RECORDS` with over 250 real historical records for training. I plan to train and test a decision tree / gradient boosted ensemble regressor with an 80/20 split and display R^2, MAE, RMSE and samples counts. I\'ll include transparently listed inputs. If confidence is low, I\'ll state that the model performance is insufficient. I\'ll also ensure data source visibility across the UI.\n\n\n**Defining Nutrient Gaps**\n\nI\'m now focused on implementing a \"No Vitamin C Fabrication\" rule in `nutrition_agent.ts` and `crop_planning_agent.ts`. I\'m calculating household RDA deficiencies for nutrients like Vitamin C, protein, iron, and Vitamin A. I\'ll then identify nutrient-rich crops from the IFCT 2017 dataset (e.g., tomatoes for Vitamin C). This will be combined with checking agricultural suitability based on the farmer\'s profile, and only recommending crops that are both nutritionally beneficial and agriculturally viable.\n\n\n**Implementing Nutrient Gap Handling**\n\nI\'m now implementing the explicit display for nutrient gap scenarios where no suitable crop is available, such as *\"No suitable crop was identified from the available data for this nutritional gap.\"* I am making sure this is integrated within `nutrition_agent.ts` and `crop_planning_agent.ts`.\n\n**Fixing Delete Functionality**\n\nI\'m now focused on implementing a full deletion pipeline and fixing delete buttons in `FarmProgressTracker.tsx` and `YieldTrackingModal.tsx`. I\'ll implement confirmation modals, Supabase DELETE queries with proper `user_id` enforcement, local storage purging, re-fetching data, recalculating agents, and refreshing state. I am ensuring that the Supabase tables and client methods in `SupabaseService.ts` have proper fallback handling.\n\n**Implementing Refresh Buttons**\n\nI am working on implementing refresh buttons.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 12
      nanos: 491069578
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
