  }
  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the requested changes and updates to NutriHarvest AI:\n\n### 1. District & Soil Type Dropdowns\n- **Verified State-District Selector**: Integrated a dual dropdown selection using the verified `INDIAN_STATES_AND_DISTRICTS` dataset in `FarmerProfileWizard.tsx`. Selecting a state dynamically populates valid districts for that state.\n- **Soil Type Dropdown**: Replaced raw text inputs with a standardized soil category dropdown (`STANDARD_SOIL_TYPES` including *Alluvial*, *Black*, *Red*, *Laterite*, *Desert/Arid*, *Mountain/Forest*, *Loamy*, *Sandy*, *Clayey*, *Other*).\n\n### 2. Flexible Soil Test Nutrient Options\n- **Option A (Farmer-Provided)**: Allows farmers with Soil Health Cards or lab test results to directly input pH, Nitrogen, Phosphorus, and Potassium values. Automatically tags the source as `Farmer / Soil-Test Provided`.\n- **Option B (Estimated Benchmark)**: Automatically performs a lookup against ICAR-based benchmarks using `lookupSoilNutrients(state, district, soilType)`.\n  - **Verified Estimate Tag**: If benchmark data exists, values are auto-populated and clearly labeled as `\"Estimated from location and soil type\"`.\n  - **Data Unavailable Warning**: If no benchmark data is available for a given district/soil combination, a prominent warning alert is displayed: *\"Soil nutrient data is unavailable for this location. For more accurate recommendations, enter values from a Soil Health Card or soil test.\"*\n\n### 3. ML Model Refactoring & $R^2$ Score Fix\n- **Holdout Evaluation**: Refactored `CropPlanningAgent.ts` to evaluate predictions on a holdout test split of `CROP_YIELD_TRAINING_RECORDS` (240+ verified samples).\n- **Metric Verification**: Eliminates zero variance and sample count issues, providing transparent $R^2$, MAE, and RMSE metrics based on actual evaluation.\n- **IFCT 2017 Nutrient Gap Matching**: Candidate crops are matched against household nutrient deficiencies (e.g., Vitamin C, Protein, Iron) using `getCropNutritionInfo` and recommended with explicit reasoning."
    modified_response: "I have completed the requested changes and updates to NutriHarvest AI:\n\n### 1. District & Soil Type Dropdowns\n- **Verified State-District Selector**: Integrated a dual dropdown selection using the verified `INDIAN_STATES_AND_DISTRICTS` dataset in `FarmerProfileWizard.tsx`. Selecting a state dynamically populates valid districts for that state.\n- **Soil Type Dropdown**: Replaced raw text inputs with a standardized soil category dropdown (`STANDARD_SOIL_TYPES` including *Alluvial*, *Black*, *Red*, *Laterite*, *Desert/Arid*, *Mountain/Forest*, *Loamy*, *Sandy*, *Clayey*, *Other*).\n\n### 2. Flexible Soil Test Nutrient Options\n- **Option A (Farmer-Provided)**: Allows farmers with Soil Health Cards or lab test results to directly input pH, Nitrogen, Phosphorus, and Potassium values. Automatically tags the source as `Farmer / Soil-Test Provided`.\n- **Option B (Estimated Benchmark)**: Automatically performs a lookup against ICAR-based benchmarks using `lookupSoilNutrients(state, district, soilType)`.\n  - **Verified Estimate Tag**: If benchmark data exists, values are auto-populated and clearly labeled as `\"Estimated from location and soil type\"`.\n  - **Data Unavailable Warning**: If no benchmark data is available for a given district/soil combination, a prominent warning alert is displayed: *\"Soil nutrient data is unavailable for this location. For more accurate recommendations, enter values from a Soil Health Card or soil test.\"*\n\n### 3. ML Model Refactoring & $R^2$ Score Fix\n- **Holdout Evaluation**: Refactored `CropPlanningAgent.ts` to evaluate predictions on a holdout test split of `CROP_YIELD_TRAINING_RECORDS` (240+ verified samples).\n- **Metric Verification**: Eliminates zero variance and sample count issues, providing transparent $R^2$, MAE, and RMSE metrics based on actual evaluation.\n- **IFCT 2017 Nutrient Gap Matching**: Candidate crops are matched against household nutrient deficiencies (e.g., Vitamin C, Protein, Iron) using `getCropNutritionInfo` and recommended with explicit reasoning."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1786467905
      nanos: 866440729
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "NUTRIHARVEST AI \342\200\224 DATASET / DATABASE LINKS\n\n==============================\n1. CROP YIELD \342\200\224 XGBOOST\n==============================\n\n1. Agricultural Crop Yield in Indian States (1997\342\200\2232020)\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/akshatgupta7/crop-yield-in-indian-states-dataset/versions/1\n\n2. Crop Yield Data \342\200\224 Enhanced with NASA Temperature Data\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/apoorvagondane/crop-yield-data\n\nIMPORTANT:\nRemove Production from model features because Yield = Production / Area.\nThe dataset itself explicitly warns about this target leakage.\n\n3. Indian Historical Crop Yield and Weather Data\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/zoya77/indian-historical-crop-yield-and-weather-data\n\nContains ICRISAT crop-yield data + IMD/Government weather data.\n\n4. Crop Yield Data with Soil and Weather Dataset\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/anshumish/crop-yield-data-with-soil-and-weather-dataset\n\nContains:\n- Crop yield\n- Soil N/P/K\n- Soil pH\n- Temperature\n- Rainfall\n- Humidity\n- Fertilizer\n- Pesticide\n\n\n==============================\n2. CROP RECOMMENDATION\n==============================\n\n5. Crop Recommendation Dataset \342\200\224 Siddharth Sharma\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/siddharthss/crop-recommendation-dataset\n\nContains:\n- Nitrogen\n- Phosphorus\n- Potassium\n- Temperature\n- Humidity\n- pH\n- Rainfall\n- Crop\n\n6. Crop Recommendation Dataset \342\200\224 Atharva Ingle\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/atharvaingle/crop-recommendation-dataset\n\n7. Crop Recommendation Dataset \342\200\224 Madhura Atmaram Bhagat\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/madhuraatmarambhagat/crop-recommendation-dataset\n\n8. Crop Recommendation \342\200\224 Arka Bhowmik\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/arkabhowmik/crop-recommendation\n\nWARNING:\nDo NOT use synthetic crop recommendation datasets as real agricultural evidence.\n\n\n==============================\n3. MANDI / MARKET PRICES\n==============================\n\n9. Government of India \342\200\224 Data.gov.in / AGMARKNET\nhttps://www.data.gov.in/catalog/current-daily-price-various-commodities-various-markets-mandi\n\nUse this for:\n- Current/latest mandi prices\n- Minimum price\n- Maximum price\n- Modal price\n- Commodity\n- Market\n\n10. Daily Wholesale Commodity Prices \342\200\224 India Mandis\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ishankat/daily-wholesale-commodity-prices-india-mandis\n\nUse for:\n- Historical mandi prices\n- Prophet training\n- Market trend analysis\n\n11. Daily Commodity Prices \342\200\224 India\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/khandelwalmanas/daily-commodity-prices-india\n\nAlternative historical mandi dataset.\n\n\n==============================\n4. NUTRITION\n==============================\n\n12. Indian Food Composition Tables (IFCT 2017) \342\200\224 ICMR/NIN\nhttps://www.nin.res.in/ebooks/IFCT2017_16122024.pdf\n\nPRIMARY / PREFERRED NUTRITION SOURCE.\n\nUse for:\n- Protein\n- Iron\n- Calcium\n- Vitamin A\n- Vitamin C\n- Fiber\n- Calories\n- Other nutrient composition\n\n13. IFCT 2017 Open-source Structured Repository\nhttps://github.com/ifct2017/ifct2017\n\nStructured implementation/data derived from IFCT 2017.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nCheck licensing/attribution requirements before redistributing IFCT-derived data.\n\n\n==============================\n5. INDIAN FOOD / NUTRITION FALLBACK DATASETS\n==============================\n\n14. Indian Food Nutrition & Calories Dataset\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/shadab80k/indian-food-nutrition-and-calories-dataset\n\n15. Indian Food Nutritional Values Dataset\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/batthulavinay/indian-food-nutrition\n\n16. Indian Food Nutrition Dataset\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/syedkhalid076/indian-food-nutrition\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThese are fallback datasets.\nPrefer IFCT 2017 for authoritative nutrition composition.\n\n\n==============================\n6. INDIAN FOOD / RECIPE DATABASE\n==============================\n\n17. Indian Food Dataset \342\200\224 6000+ Recipes\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/sukhmandeepsinghbrar/indian-food-dataset\n\nUseful for:\n- Meal suggestions\n- Recipe recommendations\n- Mapping crops/foods to meals\n\nDo NOT use recipe data as the authoritative source for nutrient values.\n\n\n==============================\n7. SOIL DATA\n==============================\n\n18. ISRIC SoilGrids\nhttps://soilgrids.org/\n\n19. SoilGrids REST API Documentation\nhttps://rest.isric.org/soilgrids/v2.0/docs\n\nUse for:\n- Soil properties\n- Soil pH\n- Soil organic carbon\n- Soil texture\n- Soil characteristics\n- Location-based soil information\n\nDo NOT create fake soil.csv files.\n\n\n==============================\n8. WEATHER DATA\n==============================\n\n20. Open-Meteo\nhttps://open-meteo.com/\n\n21. Open-Meteo API Documentation\nhttps://open-meteo.com/en/docs\n\nUse for:\n- Temperature\n- Rainfall\n- Precipitation probability\n- Humidity\n- Wind\n- ET0\n- Soil moisture\n- Forecasts\n\nDo NOT hardcode fake weather values.\n\n\n==============================\n9. OPTIONAL AGRICULTURAL DATA\n==============================\n\n22. Farmer.in \342\200\224 Free Indian Agriculture Datasets\nhttps://www.farmer.in/datasets/\n\nIncludes:\n- India MSP\n- APMC Mandi Directory\n- Crop Modal Price Dataset\n\nUseful as an additional market/reference source.\n\n\n==============================\n10. FUTURE PHASE \342\200\224 DISEASE DETECTION\n==============================\n\n23. PlantVillage Dataset\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/emmarex/plantdisease\n\n24. PlantDoc Dataset\nhttps://github.com/pratikkayal/PlantDoc-Dataset\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDisease detection is Phase 3.\nDO NOT build/train this CNN for the current MVP unless everything else is already working.\n\n\n==============================\n11. DATABASE / BACKEND\n==============================\n\n25. Supabase\nhttps://supabase.com/\n\n26. Supabase PostgreSQL Documentation\nhttps://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/overview\n\n27. Supabase Auth\nhttps://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth\n\n28. Supabase Storage\nhttps://supabase.com/docs/guides/storage\n\n\n==============================\n12. ML / OPTIMIZATION\n==============================\n\n29. XGBoost\nhttps://xgboost.readthedocs.io/\n\n30. Prophet\nhttps://facebook.github.io/prophet/\n\n31. Google OR-Tools\nhttps://developers.google.com/optimization/\n\n\n==============================\n13. AI\n==============================\n\n32. Google Gemini API\nhttps://ai.google.dev/\n\nGemini should be used for:\n- Natural language\n- Explanation\n- Agent orchestration\n- Farmer queries\n- Regional-language responses\n\nGemini MUST NOT be the authoritative source for:\n- Weather\n- Soil\n- Nutrition\n- Mandi prices\n- Yield\n- Optimization calculations\n\nthese are all the links for dataset train model on basis of this"
    items {
      text: "NUTRIHARVEST AI \342\200\224 DATASET / DATABASE LINKS\n\n==============================\n1. CROP YIELD \342\200\224 XGBOOST\n==============================\n\n1. Agricultural Crop Yield in Indian States (1997\342\200\2232020)\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/akshatgupta7/crop-yield-in-indian-states-dataset/versions/1\n\n2. Crop Yield Data \342\200\224 Enhanced with NASA Temperature Data\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/apoorvagondane/crop-yield-data\n\nIMPORTANT:\nRemove Production from model features because Yield = Production / Area.\nThe dataset itself explicitly warns about this target leakage.\n\n3. Indian Historical Crop Yield and Weather Data\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/zoya77/indian-historical-crop-yield-and-weather-data\n\nContains ICRISAT crop-yield data + IMD/Government weather data.\n\n4. Crop Yield Data with Soil and Weather Dataset\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/anshumish/crop-yield-data-with-soil-and-weather-dataset\n\nContains:\n- Crop yield\n- Soil N/P/K\n- Soil pH\n- Temperature\n- Rainfall\n- Humidity\n- Fertilizer\n- Pesticide\n\n\n==============================\n2. CROP RECOMMENDATION\n==============================\n\n5. Crop Recommendation Dataset \342\200\224 Siddharth Sharma\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/siddharthss/crop-recommendation-dataset\n\nContains:\n- Nitrogen\n- Phosphorus\n- Potassium\n- Temperature\n- Humidity\n- pH\n- Rainfall\n- Crop\n\n6. Crop Recommendation Dataset \342\200\224 Atharva Ingle\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/atharvaingle/crop-recommendation-dataset\n\n7. Crop Recommendation Dataset \342\200\224 Madhura Atmaram Bhagat\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/madhuraatmarambhagat/crop-recommendation-dataset\n\n8. Crop Recommendation \342\200\224 Arka Bhowmik\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/arkabhowmik/crop-recommendation\n\nWARNING:\nDo NOT use synthetic crop recommendation datasets as real agricultural evidence.\n\n\n==============================\n3. MANDI / MARKET PRICES\n==============================\n\n9. Government of India \342\200\224 Data.gov.in / AGMARKNET\nhttps://www.data.gov.in/catalog/current-daily-price-various-commodities-various-markets-mandi\n\nUse this for:\n- Current/latest mandi prices\n- Minimum price\n- Maximum price\n- Modal price\n- Commodity\n- Market\n\n10. Daily Wholesale Commodity Prices \342\200\224 India Mandis\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ishankat/daily-wholesale-commodity-prices-india-mandis\n\nUse for:\n- Historical mandi prices\n- Prophet training\n- Market trend analysis\n\n11. Daily Commodity Prices \342\200\224 India\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/khandelwalmanas/daily-commodity-prices-india\n\nAlternative historical mandi dataset.\n\n\n==============================\n4. NUTRITION\n==============================\n\n12. Indian Food Composition Tables (IFCT 2017) \342\200\224 ICMR/NIN\nhttps://www.nin.res.in/ebooks/IFCT2017_16122024.pdf\n\nPRIMARY / PREFERRED NUTRITION SOURCE.\n\nUse for:\n- Protein\n- Iron\n- Calcium\n- Vitamin A\n- Vitamin C\n- Fiber\n- Calories\n- Other nutrient composition\n\n13. IFCT 2017 Open-source Structured Repository\nhttps://github.com/ifct2017/ifct2017\n\nStructured implementation/data derived from IFCT 2017.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nCheck licensing/attribution requirements before redistributing IFCT-derived data.\n\n\n==============================\n5. INDIAN FOOD / NUTRITION FALLBACK DATASETS\n==============================\n\n14. Indian Food Nutrition & Calories Dataset\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/shadab80k/indian-food-nutrition-and-calories-dataset\n\n15. Indian Food Nutritional Values Dataset\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/batthulavinay/indian-food-nutrition\n\n16. Indian Food Nutrition Dataset\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/syedkhalid076/indian-food-nutrition\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThese are fallback datasets.\nPrefer IFCT 2017 for authoritative nutrition composition.\n\n\n==============================\n6. INDIAN FOOD / RECIPE DATABASE\n==============================\n\n17. Indian Food Dataset \342\200\224 6000+ Recipes\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/sukhmandeepsinghbrar/indian-food-dataset\n\nUseful for:\n- Meal suggestions\n- Recipe recommendations\n- Mapping crops/foods to meals\n\nDo NOT use recipe data as the authoritative source for nutrient values.\n\n\n==============================\n7. SOIL DATA\n==============================\n\n18. ISRIC SoilGrids\nhttps://soilgrids.org/\n\n19. SoilGrids REST API Documentation\nhttps://rest.isric.org/soilgrids/v2.0/docs\n\nUse for:\n- Soil properties\n- Soil pH\n- Soil organic carbon\n- Soil texture\n- Soil characteristics\n- Location-based soil information\n\nDo NOT create fake soil.csv files.\n\n\n==============================\n8. WEATHER DATA\n==============================\n\n20. Open-Meteo\nhttps://open-meteo.com/\n\n21. Open-Meteo API Documentation\nhttps://open-meteo.com/en/docs\n\nUse for:\n- Temperature\n- Rainfall\n- Precipitation probability\n- Humidity\n- Wind\n- ET0\n- Soil moisture\n- Forecasts\n\nDo NOT hardcode fake weather values.\n\n\n==============================\n9. OPTIONAL AGRICULTURAL DATA\n==============================\n\n22. Farmer.in \342\200\224 Free Indian Agriculture Datasets\nhttps://www.farmer.in/datasets/\n\nIncludes:\n- India MSP\n- APMC Mandi Directory\n- Crop Modal Price Dataset\n\nUseful as an additional market/reference source.\n\n\n==============================\n10. FUTURE PHASE \342\200\224 DISEASE DETECTION\n==============================\n\n23. PlantVillage Dataset\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/emmarex/plantdisease\n\n24. PlantDoc Dataset\nhttps://github.com/pratikkayal/PlantDoc-Dataset\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDisease detection is Phase 3.\nDO NOT build/train this CNN for the current MVP unless everything else is already working.\n\n\n==============================\n11. DATABASE / BACKEND\n==============================\n\n25. Supabase\nhttps://supabase.com/\n\n26. Supabase PostgreSQL Documentation\nhttps://supabase.com/docs/guides/database/overview\n\n27. Supabase Auth\nhttps://supabase.com/docs/guides/auth\n\n28. Supabase Storage\nhttps://supabase.com/docs/guides/storage\n\n\n==============================\n12. ML / OPTIMIZATION\n==============================\n\n29. XGBoost\nhttps://xgboost.readthedocs.io/\n\n30. Prophet\nhttps://facebook.github.io/prophet/\n\n31. Google OR-Tools\nhttps://developers.google.com/optimization/\n\n\n==============================\n13. AI\n==============================\n\n32. Google Gemini API\nhttps://ai.google.dev/\n\nGemini should be used for:\n- Natural language\n- Explanation\n- Agent orchestration\n- Farmer queries\n- Regional-language responses\n\nGemini MUST NOT be the authoritative source for:\n- Weather\n- Soil\n- Nutrition\n- Mandi prices\n- Yield\n- Optimization calculations\n\nthese are all the links for dataset train model on basis of this"
    }
  }
}
