he held-out test set.\n\n14. Report the actual minimum, maximum, mean and median of the target yield in the test set.\n\n15. Compare the XGBoost model against a simple baseline model such as predicting the mean training-set yield.\n\n16. Report:\nModel R\302\262\nBaseline R\302\262\nModel MAE\nBaseline MAE\nModel RMSE\nBaseline RMSE\n\n17. Check whether the 48 test samples are independent from the training samples.\n\n18. If multiple records belong to the same crop/location/year/farm, check whether random splitting caused information from the same group to appear in both training and test sets.\n\nIf this is possible, use an appropriate grouped or time-based split instead.\n\n19. Tell me whether R\302\262 = 0.886 is trustworthy based on this audit.\n\n20. If it is NOT trustworthy, explain exactly why and do not hide the problem.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nDo NOT change the displayed R\302\262 to make the model look better.\n\nDo NOT fabricate data.\n\nDo NOT generate synthetic rows just to increase the number of samples.\n\nDo NOT manipulate the test set.\n\nDo NOT claim the model is accurate simply because R\302\262 is high.\n\nI want an honest technical audit first.\n\nAt the end, give me:\n\nVERDICT:\n- TRUSTWORTHY\nor\n- NOT TRUSTWORTHY\n\nand explain why."
