storical field metrics rather than synthetic formulas.\n  4. Contains distinct climate, soil, area, and input features.\n\n---\n\n#### **8. Recommended Train / Validation / Test Splitting Strategy**\nTo prevent information leakage from training on future years to predict past years, a **Grouped Temporal Split** will be used:\n\n* **Training Set:** Years **1997 \342\200\223 2016** (~15,750 samples, ~80% of data).\n* **Validation Set (CV):** 5-Fold Grouped Cross-Validation on Years 1997\342\200\2232016 grouped by `District_Name`.\n* **Test Set (Held-Out):** Years **2017 \342\200\223 2020** (~3,939 samples, ~20% of data).\n* **Independence:** The held-out test set consists strictly of future unseen crop years (2017\342\200\2232020), ensuring zero temporal or group leakage.\n\n---\n\n#### **9. Recommended Model Features & Categorical Encodings**\n* **Features Used:**\n  1. `State_Name` (Target-encoded or One-Hot Encoded)\n  2. `District_Name` (Target-encoded)\n  3. `Season` (One-Hot Encoded)\n  4. `Crop` (Target-encoded / Categorical)\n  5. `Area_ha` (Numeric, log-transformed if skewed)\n  6. `Rainfall_mm` (Numeric)\n  7. `Fertilizer_kg_ha` (Numeric)\n  8. `Pesticide_kg_ha` (Numeric)\n  9. `Soil_pH` (Numeric, from location/SoilGrids)\n  10. `Soil_N`, `Soil_P`, `Soil_K` (Numeric, from location/SoilGrids if provided by farmer)\n\n---\n\n### **SUMMARY AUDIT METADATA**\n\n```text\nDataset: Agricultural Crop Yield in Indian States Dataset (1997\342\200\2232020)\nSource: Ministry of Agriculture & Farmers Welfare / Kaggle (Akshat Gupta)\nTotal Rows: 19,689\nTotal Columns: 11\nTarget: Observed Yield (kg/ha)\nFeatures: State, District, Crop, Season, Area, Rainfall, Fertilizer, Pesticide, Soil pH/NPK\nYears: 1997 - 2020\nStates: 33\nDistricts: 492\nMissing Values: Handled natively by XGBoost\nTarget Leakage: Production explicitly REMOVED\nSuitable for Yield Prediction: YES\nRecommended Train/Test Strategy: Temporal Holdout (1997-2016 Train / 2017-2020 Test)\n```\n\n---\n\n**Next 