    response: "Here is the updated audit report addressing soil data capabilities, pre-season vs. in-season prediction modes, temporal validation splits, feature availability, and target leakage safeguards.\n\n---\n\n### **PRE-IMPLEMENTATION AUDIT & FEATURE DISCIPLINE REPORT**\n\n#### **1. Soil Data Property Capabilities (SoilGrids Correction)**\n* **SoilGrids REST API v2.0 Scope**: Returns `pH (water)`, `Nitrogen (cg/kg)`, `Soil Organic Carbon (dg/kg)`, `Sand (%)`, `Silt (%)`, `Clay (%)`, `Bulk Density (cg/cm\302\263)`.\n* **Phosphorus (P) and Potassium (K) Handling**:\n  * SoilGrids **does not mapped P and K**.\n  * P & K will **only** be populated if provided directly by the farmer via a Soil Health Card or lab test.\n  * If unavailable, P and K are left as missing (`undefined`) or handled by tree missing-split logic, clearly marked in the UI as **\"Parameter unavailable without soil test report\"**.\n* **Source Labeling**:\n  * SoilGrids properties $\\rightarrow$ **\"Location-based soil estimate (SoilGrids REST API)\"**\n  * Lab entries $\\rightarrow$ **\"Farmer / Soil-Test Provided\"**\n\n---\n\n#### **2. Pre-Season vs. In-Season Prediction Modes**\n\n| Prediction Mode | Mode Description | Features Used at Prediction Time | Label Displayed to Farmer |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **PRE-SEASON** | Generated before or at planting | State, District, Crop, Season, Farm Area, Pre-season Soil pH & N (SoilGrids/Test), **Historical 10-Year Average Seasonal Rainfall**, **Planned Fertilizer Rate** | `Pre-season ML Yield Estimate` |\n| **IN-SEASON** | Updated after planting during crop growth | All Pre-Season features + **Actual Cumulative Rainfall-to-Date** (Open-Meteo API), **Live Weather/Temp**, **Actual Fertilizer & Pesticide Applied** | `In-season Updated ML Estimate` |\n\n---\n\n#### **3. Temporal Validation Split Strategy**\n\n```text\nFull Dataset (1997 - 2020: 19,689 rows)\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Training Set (1997 \342\200\223 2015): ~14,800 samples (~75%)\n\342\224\202     \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Internal Model Selection: 5-Fold Grouped/Rolling Time-Series CV (1997-2015)\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Validation Set (2016): ~1,200 samples (~6%)\n\342\224\202     \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Hyperparameter Tuning & Out-of-Fold Early Stopping\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 Final Held-Out Test Set (2017 \342\200\223 2020): ~3,689 samples (~19%)\n      \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 ZERO Leakage: Strictly evaluates generalization on future unseen crop years\n```\n\n---\n\n#### **4. Target Encoding Safeguards**\n* Target encoding statistics (mean target per crop, district, and state) are **fitted ONLY on the 1997\342\200\2232015 training set**.\n* Validation (2016) and Test (2017\342\200\2232020) target values are **100% hidden** from the encoder during fitting to prevent target leakage.\n\n---\n\n#### **5. Baseline Benchmarks for Evaluation**\nThe trained XGBoost model performance will be evaluated on the 2017\342\200\2232020 held-out test set against **two** baselines:\n1. **Global Mean Predictor**: Predicts global training target mean ($\\bar{y}_{\\text{train}}$) for all samples.\n2. **Crop-Specific Historical Mean Predictor**: Predicts historical average yield per specific crop ($\\bar{y}_{\\text{crop}}$) from the training period.\n\n---\n\n#### **6. Model Reliability & Error Disclosure in UI**\n* Yield predictions will be displayed alongside explicit uncertainty bounds:\n  * **Estimated Yield**: e.g., $3,450 \\text{ kg/ha}$\n  * **Model Error Metric**: $MAE = \\pm 380 \\text{ kg/ha}$\n  * **Disclaimer Tag**: *\"ML estimate based on historical 1997\342\200\2232020 yield model. Actual yield depends on local weather events, pest outbreaks, and field management.\"*\n\n---\n\n#### **7. Final Feature Availability & Leakage Matrix**\n\n| Feature | Source | Available Pre-Season? | Available In-Season? | Leakage Risk & Safeguard |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :---: | :--- |\n| `State_Name` | Farmer Profile | **Yes** | **Yes** | **No Risk** (Location parameter) |\n| `District_Name` | Farmer Profile | **Yes** | **Yes** | **No Risk** (Agro-climatic zone) |\n| `Crop` | Farmer Choice | **Yes** | **Yes** | **No Risk** (Target category) |\n| `Season` | Planting Time | **Yes** | **Yes** | **No Risk** (Kharif/Rabi/Zaid) |\n| `Area_ha` | Farmer Profile | **Yes** | **Yes** | **Checked**: Area is an input variable. Models evaluated with & without Area to verify no proxy leakage. |\n| `Soil_pH` | SoilGrids API / Soil Test | **Yes** | **Yes** | **No Risk** (Physical soil property) |\n| `Soil_N` | SoilGrids API / Soil Test | **Yes** | **Yes** | **No Risk** (Total nitrogen content) |\n| `Soil_P` | Soil Test / Missing | **If Test Provided** | **If Test Provided** | **No Risk**: Never fabricated. Left as missing if no test provided. |\n| `Soil_K` | Soil Test / Missing | **If Test Provided** | **If Test Provided** | **No Risk**: Never fabricated. Left as missing if no test provided. |\n| `Rainfall_mm` | Historical Avg / Open-Meteo | **Yes (Historical Avg)** | **Yes (Actual-to-Date)** | **Prevented**: Pre-season uses historical climate mean. In-season uses actual Open-Meteo API data. |\n| `Fertilizer_kg_ha` | Farmer Planned / Applied | **Yes (Planned)** | **Yes (Actual Applied)** | **Prevented**: Pre-season uses farmer\'s planned budget rate. In-season uses actual log. |\n| `Pesticide_kg_ha` | Farmer Planned / Applied | **Yes (Planned)** | **Yes (Actual Applied)** | **Prevented**: Pre-season uses planned application rate. In-season uses actual log. |\n| `Production` | Harvest Report | **NO** | **NO** | **REMOVED (CRITICAL LEAKAGE)**: $Yield = \\frac{Production}{Area}$. Completely excluded. |\n\n---\n\n**Confirmation Request:** The feature availability, pre-season vs in-season distinction, SoilGrids limitation, and temporal validation splits are audited and ready. Please confirm to proceed with implementing this real XGBoost ML pipeline and dataset update."
    modified_response: "Here is the updated audit report addressing soil data capabilities, pre-season vs. in-season prediction modes, temporal validation splits, feature availability, and target leakage safeguards.\n\n---\n\n### **PRE-IMPLEMENTATION AUDIT & FEATURE DISCIPLINE REPORT**\n\n#### **1. Soil Data Property Capabilities (SoilGrids Correction)**\n* **SoilGrids REST API v2.0 Scope**: Returns `pH (water)`, `Nitrogen (cg/kg)`, `Soil Organic Carbon (dg/kg)`, `Sand (%)`, `Silt (%)`, `Clay (%)`, `Bulk Density (cg/cm\302\263)`.\n* **Phosphorus (P) and Potassium (K) Handling**:\n  * SoilGrids **does not mapped P and K**.\n  * P & K will **only** be populated if provided directly by the farmer via a Soil Health Card or lab test.\n  * If unavailable, P and K are left as missing (`undefined`) or handled by tree missing-split logic, clearly marked in the UI as **\"Parameter unavailable without soil test report\"**.\n* **Source Labeling**:\n  * SoilGrids properties $\\rightarrow$ **\"Location-based soil estimate (SoilGrids REST API)\"**\n  * Lab entries $\\rightarrow$ **\"Farmer / Soil-Test Provided\"**\n\n---\n\n#### **2. Pre-Season vs. In-Season Prediction Modes**\n\n| Prediction Mode | Mode Description | Features Used at Prediction Time | Label Displayed to Farmer |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **PRE-SEASON** | Generated before or at planting | State, District, Crop, Season, Farm Area, Pre-season Soil pH & N (SoilGrids/Test), **Historical 10-Year Average Seasonal Rainfall**, **Planned Fertilizer Rate** | `Pre-season ML Yield Estimate` |\n| **IN-SEASON** | Updated after planting during crop growth | All Pre-Season features + **Actual Cumulative Rainfall-to-Date** (Open-Meteo API), **Live Weather/Temp**, **Actual Fertilizer & Pesticide Applied** | `In-season Updated ML Estimate` |\n\n---\n\n#### **3. Temporal Validation Split Strategy**\n\n```text\nFull Dataset (1997 - 2020: 19,689 rows)\n\342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Training Set (1997 \342\2