steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1786469165
      nanos: 146875472
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Proceed with implementing the REAL XGBoost crop-yield ML pipeline based on the approved audit.\n\nHowever, follow these final requirements strictly:\n\n1. REMOVE the existing synthetic dataset and synthetic yield generator completely.\n\nRemove:\n- pseudoRandom()\n- cropBaseYields\n- formula-generated yields\n- predictYieldInternal() heuristic\n- synthetic training records\n- fake model metrics\n\n2. Use the verified real Agricultural Crop Yield in Indian States dataset:\n\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/akshatgupta7/crop-yield-in-indian-states-dataset\n\nDo not fabricate or augment the dataset.\n\n3. Before training, verify the actual downloaded dataset contents against the audit.\n\nReport:\n- Rows\n- Columns\n- Years\n- States\n- Districts\n- Crops\n- Missing values\n- Target\n- Potential leakage\n\nIf the downloaded dataset differs materially from the audit, STOP and report the differences rather than silently proceeding.\n\n4. Target:\n\nYield in kg/ha.\n\nProduction MUST NOT be used as a feature.\n\n5. Use the temporal structure:\n\nTraining:\n1997\342\200\2232015\n\nValidation:\n2016\n\nFinal held-out test:\n2017\342\200\2232020\n\nThe 2017\342\200\2232020 test set must remain completely untouched until final evaluation.\n\nDo not use test results for hyperparameter tuning.\n\n6. Historical features must obey \"information available at prediction time.\"\n\nFor every historical statistic, verify that it only uses data available before the prediction year.\n\nFor example, a 2017 prediction must NOT use 2018\342\200\2232020 information to calculate historical averages.\n\n7. PRE-SEASON MODEL\n\nUse only features that would genuinely be known before planting:\n\n- State\n- District\n- Crop\n- Season\n- Area\n- Soil pH\n- Soil N\n- Historical climate information\n- Planned fertilizer\n- Planned pesticide if appropriate\n\nDo not use future rainfall or future actual farm inputs.\n\n8. IN-SEASON MODEL\n\nAllow updates using information that has actually become available:\n\n- Actual cumulative rainfall\n- Live weather\n- Actual fertilizer application\n- Actual pesticide application\n- Irrigation\n- Crop growth information\n\nClearly label these predictions as:\n\n\"Pre-season ML Yield Estimate\"\n\nor\n\n\"In-season Updated ML Yield Estimate\"\n\n9. SOIL DATA\n\nUse SoilGrids only for properties it actually provides.\n\nDo NOT invent P or K.\n\nP/K should come from:\n- Farmer\'s Soil Health Card\n- Laboratory soil test\n- Another verified source\n\nIf unavailable, leave them missing and ensure the model handles missing values appropriately.\n\nClearly label SoilGrids information:\n\n\"Location-based soil estimate\"\n\nand soil-test information:\n\n\"Farmer/Soil-Test Provided\"\n\n10. TRAIN A REAL XGBOOST REGRESSOR.\n\nThe prediction must come from the trained model, not a TypeScript mathematical formula.\n\n11. TARGET ENCODING\n\nIf target encoding is used for State, District, or Crop:\n\n- Fit encoders only on the training portion.\n- Never use validation/test target values.\n- Refit encoding correctly inside each CV fold.\n- Prevent leakage through preprocessing pipelines.\n\n12. MODEL VALIDATION\n\nUse appropriate time-aware validation within the training period.\n\nEvaluate the final model ONLY once on the untouched 2017\342\200\2232020 test set.\n\nReport:\n\n- R\302\262\n- MAE\n- RMSE\n\nAlso report:\n\n- Number of training samples\n- Number of validation samples\n- Number of test samples\n- Cross-validation results\n\n13. BASELINES\n\nCompare against:\n\nA. Global training mean\n\nB. Crop-specific historical mean calculated ONLY from the training period.\n\nReport model vs baseline performance.\n\n14. PER-CROP PERFORMANCE\n\nIn addition to overall metrics, calculate performance for crops with sufficient test samples:\n\n- R\302\262\n- MAE\n- RMSE\n- Number of test samples\n\nThis prevents a high overall R\302\262 from hiding poor performance on individual crops.\n\n15. DO NOT FABRICATE METRICS.\n\nIf the real model performs poorly, display the poor result.\n\nDo not:\n- Manipulate test data\n- Generate synthetic rows\n- Artificially improve R\302\262\n- Remove difficult samples\n- Modify metrics\n- Create fake confidence scores\n\n16. PREDICTION UNCERTAINTY\n\nDo not display arbitrary \"confidence percentages.\"\n\nIf uncertainty intervals are implemented, explain exactly how they were calculated.\n\nOtherwise display the model\'s historical error metrics instead.\n\n17. APPLICATION INTEGRATION\n\nAfter the model is genuinely trained and validated, connect it to the farmer\'s real profile.\n\nUse:\n\nFarmer data\n+\nVerified soil data\n+\nHistorical climate\n+\nLive weather where appropriate\n+\nActual farm records\n\342\206\223\nReal XGBoost model\n\342\206\223\nYield estimate\n\n18. MODEL VERSIONING\n\nStore:\n\n- Dataset version/source\n- Training date\n- Feature list\n- Model type\n- Hyperparameters\n- Training period\n- Test period\n- R\302\262\n- MAE\n- RMSE\n\n19. UI\n\nReplace the current fake model metrics with the actual metrics from the newly trained model.\n\nClearly label:\n\n\"Real historical dataset\"\n\n\"ML prediction\"\n\n\"Historical model error\"\n\n\"Actual farmer yield\"\n\nDo not present predicted yield as guaranteed.\n\n20. ACTUAL YIELD FEEDBACK\n\nWhen the farmer later enters actual harvested yield:\n\nStore:\n\nPredicted yield\nActual yield\nPrediction date\nCrop\nDistrict\nSeason\nRelevant model inputs\n\nThen calculate:\n\nPrediction error = Actual yield - Predicted yield\n\nUse this historical farmer data for tracking and future analysis, but DO NOT automatically retrain the production model on one farmer\'s data without proper validation.\n\n21. FINAL SAFETY RULE\n\nIf any required real dataset, API, or model dependency cannot be accessed:\n\nSTOP and clearly report the missing dependency.\n\nDo NOT replace it with:\n- Fake data\n- Random data\n- Synthetic data\n- Hardcoded values\n- Placeholder model results\n\nThe previous R\302\262 = 0.886 from the synthetic model is INVALID and must not be displayed anywhere as the model\'s accuracy.\n\nProceed with the implementation only after verifying that the new pipeline uses the REAL dataset and a REAL trained XGBoost model."
    items {
      text: "Proceed with implementing the REAL XGBoost crop-yield ML pipeline based on the approved audit.\n\nHowever, follow these final requirements strictly:\n\n1. REMOVE the existing synthetic dataset and synthetic yield generator completely.\n\nRemove:\n- pseudoRandom()\n- cropBaseYields\n- formula-generated yields\n- predictYieldInternal() heuristic\n- synthetic training records\n- fake model metrics\n\n2. Use the verified real Agricultural Crop Yield in Indian States dataset:\n\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/akshatgupta7/crop-yield-in-indian-states-dataset\n\nDo not fabricate or augment the dataset.\n\n3. Before training, verify the actual downloaded dataset contents against the audit.\n\nReport:\n- Rows\n- Columns\n- Years\n- States\n- Districts\n- Crops\n- Missing values\n- Target\n- Potential leakage\n\nIf the downloaded dataset differs materially from the audit, STOP and report the differences rather than silently proceeding.\n\n4. Target:\n\nYield in kg/ha.\n\nProduction MUST NOT be used as a feature.\n\n5. Use the temporal structure:\n\nTraining:\n1997\342\200\2232015\n\nValidation:\n2016\n\nFinal held-out test:\n2017\342\200\2232020\n\nThe 2017\342\200\2232020 test set must remain completely untouched until final evaluation.\n\nDo not use test results for hyperparameter tuning.\n\n6. Historical features must obey \"information available at prediction time.\"\n\nFor every historical statistic, verify that it only uses data available before the prediction year.\n\nFor example, a 2017 prediction must NOT use 2018\342\200\2232020 information to calculate historical averages.\n\n7. PRE-SEASON MODEL\n\nUse only features that would genuinely be known before planting:\n\n- State\n- District\n- Crop\n- Season\n- Area\n- Soil pH\n- Soil N\n- Historical climate information\n- Planned fertilizer\n- Planned pesticide if appropriate\n\nDo not use future rainfall or future actual farm inputs.\n\n8. IN-SEASON MODEL\n\nAllow updates using information that has actually become available:\n\n- Actual cumulative rainfall\n- Live weather\n- Actual fertilizer application\n- Actual pesticide application\n- Irrigation\n- Crop growth information\n\nClearly label these predictions as:\n\n\"Pre-season ML Yield Estimate\"\n\nor\n\n\"In-season Updated ML Yield Estimate\"\n\n9. SOIL DATA\n\nUse SoilGrids only for properties it actually provides.\n\nDo NOT invent P or K.\n\nP/K should come from:\n- Farmer\'s Soil Health Card\n- Laboratory soil test\n- Another verified source\n\nIf unavailable, leave them missing and ensure the model handles missing values appropriately.\n\nClearly label SoilGrids information:\n\n\"Location-based soil estimate\"\n\nand soil-test information:\n\n\"Farmer/Soil-Test Provided\"\n\n10. TRAIN A REAL XGBOOST REGRESSOR.\n\nThe prediction must come from the trained model, not a TypeScript mathematical formula.\n\n11. TARGET ENCODING\n\nIf target encoding is used for State, District, or Crop:\n\n- Fit encoders only on the training portion.\n- Never use validation/test target values.\n- Refit encoding correctly inside each CV fold.\n- Prevent leakage through preprocessing pipelines.\n\n12. MODEL VALIDATION\n\nUse appropriate time-aware validation within the training period.\n\nEvaluate the final model ONLY once on the untouched 2017\342\200\2232020 test set.\n\nReport:\n\n- R\302\262\n- MAE\n- RMSE\n\nAlso report:\n\n- Number of training samples\n- Number of validation samples\n- Number of test samples\n- Cross-validation results\n\n13. BASELINES\n\nCompare against:\n\nA. Global training mean\n\nB. Crop-specific historical mean calculated ONLY from the training period.\n\nReport model vs baseline performance.\n\n14. PER-CROP PERFORMANCE\n\nIn addition to overall metrics, calculate performance for crops with sufficient test samples:\n\n- R\302\262\n- MAE\n- RMSE\n- Number of test samples\n\nThis prevents a high overall R\302\262 from hiding poor performance on individual crops.\n\n15. DO NOT FABRICATE METRICS.\n\nIf the real model performs poorly, display the poor result.\n\nDo not:\n- Manipulate test data\n- Generate synthetic rows\n- Artificially improve R\302\262\n- Remove difficult samples\n- Modify metrics\n- Create fake confidence scores\n\n16. PREDICTION UNCERTAINTY\n\nDo not display arbitrary \"confidence percentages.\"\n\nIf uncertainty intervals are implemented, explain exactly how they were calculated.\n\nOtherwise display the model\'s historical error metrics instead.\n\n17. APPLICATION INTEGRATION\n\nAfter the model is genuinely trained and validated, connect it to the farmer\'s real profile.\n\nUse:\n\nFarmer data\n+\nVerified soil data\n+\nHistorical climate\n+\nLive weather where appropriate\n+\nActual farm records\n\342\206\223\nReal XGBoost model\n\342\206\223\nYield estimate\n\n18. MODEL VERSIONING\n\nStore:\n\n- Dataset version/source\n- Training date\n- Feature list\n- Model type\n- Hyperparameters\n- Training period\n- Test period\n- R\302\262\n- MAE\n- RMSE\n\n19. UI\n\nReplace the current fake model metrics with the actual metrics from the newly trained model.\n\nClearly label:\n\n\"Real historical dataset\"\n\n\"ML prediction\"\n\n\"Historical model error\"\n\n\"Actual farmer yield\"\n\nDo not present predicted yield as guaranteed.\n\n20. ACTUAL YIELD FEEDBACK\n\nWhen the farmer later enters actual harvested yield:\n\nStore:\n\nPredicted yield\nActual yield\nPrediction date\nCrop\nDistrict\nSeason\nRelevant model inputs\n\nThen calculate:\n\nPrediction error = Actual yield - Predicted yield\n\nUse this historical farmer data for tracking and future analysis, but DO NOT automatically retrain the production model on one farmer\'s data without proper validation.\n\n21. FINAL SAFETY RULE\n\nIf any required real dataset, API, or model dependency cannot be accessed:\n\nSTOP and clearly report the missing dependency.\n\nDo NOT replace it with:\n- Fake data\n- Random data\n- Synthetic data\n- Hardcoded values\n- Placeholder model results\n\nThe previous R\302\262 =