  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Crop Planning Agent**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `CropPlanningAgent` and what needs to be implemented. Specifically, I\'m thinking about building a Gradient Boosted Regressor ML Engine directly from the `CROP_YIELD_TRAINING_RECORDS`. I\'ve also planned to split the dataset by year, using data up to 2015 for training.\n\n\n**Defining Validation and Test Sets**\n\nI\'ve just solidified my plan for data splitting. The 2016 data will serve as the validation set, and records from 2017 to 2020 are earmarked for the final, held-out test set. Also, I\'ve got a clearer plan for target encodings, which will be strictly calculated on the training set (1997-2015), ensuring no leakage from validation or test data.\n\n\n**Evaluating Prediction Modes**\n\nI\'m now diving into prediction modes. I\'m focusing on the `predictYield` function. The key here is differentiating pre-season versus in-season predictions using pre-planting versus live inputs, respectively. I also want to make sure the function returns a predicted yield with an error margin and a clear mode label, so I need to check all requirements for `getModelMetrics()` and `predictYield`.\n\n\n**Calculating Model Metrics**\n\nI\'m now focused on establishing the specific metrics for evaluating the Gradient Boosted Decision Trees Regressor. I\'m calculating MAE, RMSE, and R2 score for both the global mean baseline and crop-specific mean baselines on the test set. I\'ll also generate per-crop performance metrics including the number of samples, to get a good read on how the model actually does.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 29
      nanos: 197227474
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
